842
00:45:43,420 --> 00:45:48,960
If someone with an evil mind has his wish granted, the world will be consumed by evil.

843
00:45:49,440 --> 00:45:51,720
That is what has been told.

844
00:45:54,480 --> 00:46:00,460
So, the ancient sages built the Temple of Time to protect the Triforce from evil ones.

845
00:46:05,040 --> 00:46:05,660
Right.

846
00:46:10,170 --> 00:46:11,070
That's right!

847
00:46:11,370 --> 00:46:16,390
The Temple of Time is the entrance through which you can enter the sacred realm for our world.

848
00:46:17,570 --> 00:46:22,030
But the entrance is sealed with a stone wall called the Door of Time.

849
00:46:23,870 --> 00:46:28,690
and in order to open the door it is said that you need to collect three spiritual stones.

850
00:46:30,370 --> 00:46:35,050
And another thing you need is the treasure that the royal family keeps along with this legend.

851
00:46:36,790 --> 00:46:38,250
The Ocarina of Time.

852
00:46:39,210 --> 00:46:40,650
Well, you know what, lady?

853
00:46:40,650 --> 00:46:42,430
I have all of that.

854
00:46:42,670 --> 00:46:43,570
What a coincidence.

855
00:46:48,240 --> 00:46:50,600
Did you understand well the story I just told you?

856
00:46:51,340 --> 00:46:52,900
I love that they ask me this.

857
00:46:53,520 --> 00:46:56,760
Like, hey, you need to hear that again or are you good?

858
00:46:57,660 --> 00:46:58,700
I'm good, thanks!

859
00:47:00,140 --> 00:47:00,940
That's great!

860
00:47:02,140 --> 00:47:03,360
I forgot to tell you.

861
00:47:04,560 --> 00:47:06,700
I was spying through this window just now.

862
00:47:07,300 --> 00:47:08,020
Oh, yeah?

863
00:47:09,460 --> 00:47:12,400
The other element from my dream, the dark clouds.

864
00:47:12,400 --> 00:47:15,720
I believe they symbolize that man in there.

865
00:47:16,880 --> 00:47:18,520
Will he look through the window, Adam?

866
00:47:19,720 --> 00:47:20,280
No.

867
00:47:21,640 --> 00:47:22,200
Please!

868
00:47:22,240 --> 00:47:24,140
If you don't hurry, he'll be gone!

869
00:47:25,060 --> 00:47:25,620
Okay.

870
00:47:31,010 --> 00:47:32,010
Oh, yeah, that's him!

871
00:47:33,490 --> 00:47:35,450
Can you see the man with the evil eyes?

872
00:47:37,270 --> 00:47:38,570
Yes, I see the man.

873
00:47:38,930 --> 00:47:40,310
He's very evil-looking.

874
00:47:41,570 --> 00:47:45,390
That is Ganondorf, the leader of the Gerudos.

875
00:47:46,070 --> 00:47:48,010
They hail from the desert far to the west.

876
00:47:49,070 --> 00:47:49,670
Really?

877
00:47:50,590 --> 00:47:52,490
What a silly name!

878
00:47:54,410 --> 00:47:55,010
Ganondorf?

879
00:47:56,790 --> 00:47:58,310
More like Ganondork.

880
00:47:59,730 --> 00:48:03,770
Though he swears allegiance to my father, I'm sure he's not sincere.

881
00:48:04,770 --> 00:48:07,490
The dark clouds that covered Hyrule in my dream?

882
00:48:08,010 --> 00:48:09,730
They must symbolize that man.

883
00:48:12,940 --> 00:48:14,260
Oh, my God, he looked at me.

884
00:48:14,620 --> 00:48:15,160
What happened?

885
00:48:15,360 --> 00:48:15,900
Did he see you?

886
00:48:16,860 --> 00:48:17,780
No worry.

887
00:48:18,720 --> 00:48:21,480
He doesn't have any idea what we're planning yet.

888
00:48:23,880 --> 00:48:24,520
Yes.

889
00:48:25,540 --> 00:48:27,620
I told my father about my dream.

890
00:48:28,640 --> 00:48:29,900
Wait, who's your father?

891
00:48:31,140 --> 00:48:33,660
However, he didn't believe it was a prophecy.

892
00:48:34,660 --> 00:48:37,900
But, I can sense that man's evil intentions.

893
00:48:39,280 --> 00:48:39,920
Same.

894
00:48:42,120 --> 00:48:46,780
What Ganondorf is after must be nothing less than the Triforce of the Sacred Realm.

895
00:48:47,880 --> 00:48:49,880
Yes, the tree told me about this.

896
00:48:51,200 --> 00:48:53,240
He must have come to Hyrule to obtain it.

897
00:48:54,520 --> 00:48:55,720
She looks so worried.

898
00:48:56,640 --> 00:48:58,460
And, he wants to conquer Hyrule.

899
00:48:58,780 --> 00:49:00,240
No, the entire world.

900
00:49:02,820 --> 00:49:03,340
Link!

901
00:49:03,960 --> 00:49:07,300
Now, we are the only ones who can protect Hyrule.

902
00:49:08,280 --> 00:49:09,980
lady, I just showed up, okay?

903
00:49:10,180 --> 00:49:11,500
I just woke up as well.

904
00:49:12,060 --> 00:49:13,840
This is too early for this sort of thing.

905
00:49:14,780 --> 00:49:15,420
Calm down.

906
00:49:15,820 --> 00:49:16,300
Please!

907
00:49:17,320 --> 00:49:18,840
I don't believe you.

908
00:49:19,200 --> 00:49:20,420
You could be lying to me.

909
00:49:22,760 --> 00:49:23,280
Aww.

910
00:49:26,000 --> 00:49:27,700
She's so tired of my shit already.

911
00:49:28,080 --> 00:49:29,100
Please believe me.

912
00:49:29,360 --> 00:49:31,140
My prophecies have never been wrong.

913
00:49:32,260 --> 00:49:36,180
That's exactly what someone would say whose prophecies have always been wrong.

914
00:49:39,160 --> 00:49:39,680
Please!

915
00:49:40,360 --> 00:49:42,200
Okay, I'll help you.

916
00:49:43,240 --> 00:49:44,120
Thank you!

917
00:49:45,960 --> 00:49:46,480
I...

918
00:49:46,480 --> 00:49:47,140
I'm afraid!

919
00:49:47,500 --> 00:49:49,920
I have a feeling that man is gonna destroy Hyrule.

920
00:49:51,260 --> 00:49:54,340
That is a lot of, you know, insinuations here.

921
00:49:54,620 --> 00:49:56,620
You need proof to back this up, you know?

922
00:49:57,420 --> 00:49:59,260
He has such terrifying power.

923
00:50:00,740 --> 00:50:02,420
But it's fortunate that you have come.

924
00:50:02,700 --> 00:50:04,340
I mean, I guess he does have evil eyes.

925
00:50:04,700 --> 00:50:05,620
That's the proof.

926
00:50:07,240 --> 00:50:09,860
We must not let Ganondorf get the Triforce.

927
00:50:11,040 --> 00:50:13,920
I will protect the Ocarina of Time with all my power.

928
00:50:14,320 --> 00:50:15,540
He shall not have it.

929
00:50:17,020 --> 00:50:19,460
You, go find the other two spiritual stones.

930
00:50:20,800 --> 00:50:24,560
Let's get the Triforce before Ganondorf does, and then defeat him.

931
00:50:26,600 --> 00:50:27,500
One more thing.

932
00:50:27,900 --> 00:50:28,860
Take this letter.

933
00:50:29,280 --> 00:50:31,100
I'm sure it will be helpful to you.

934
00:50:31,760 --> 00:50:33,140
Oh, she's writing it now.

935
00:50:35,860 --> 00:50:37,480
You received Zelda's letter!

936
00:50:38,300 --> 00:50:38,780
Wow!

937
00:50:39,320 --> 00:50:41,440
This letter has Princess Zelda's autograph.

938
00:50:41,940 --> 00:50:43,740
Set it to C and show it with C.

939
00:50:45,720 --> 00:50:48,840
On the select item sub-screen, you can set it to...

940
00:50:48,840 --> 00:50:49,380
Okay.

941
00:50:49,700 --> 00:50:51,660
And then use that to show it to people.

942
00:50:54,100 --> 00:50:56,260
So I just go around me like, look what I got.

943
00:50:56,480 --> 00:50:57,760
I got her signature.

944
00:50:58,580 --> 00:51:00,020
I got her phone number.

945
00:51:01,420 --> 00:51:02,980
Let me look through this window again.

946
00:51:06,000 --> 00:51:06,480
Okay.

947
00:51:07,580 --> 00:51:08,500
Look what I got!

948
00:51:09,420 --> 00:51:10,220
A letter!

949
00:51:11,200 --> 00:51:13,320
It looks like this item doesn't work here.

950
00:51:13,860 --> 00:51:14,300
Oh.

951
00:51:14,780 --> 00:51:16,020
Oh, someone's standing over there.

952
00:51:16,060 --> 00:51:17,240
That's kind of...

953
00:51:17,240 --> 00:51:18,180
scary.

954
00:51:18,340 --> 00:51:18,780
Who's that?

955
00:51:21,810 --> 00:51:22,290
Zelda!

956
00:51:23,890 --> 00:51:26,150
My attendant will guide you out of the castle.

957
00:51:26,690 --> 00:51:28,170
Don't be afraid to talk to her.

958
00:51:29,790 --> 00:51:31,990
I mean, I am kind of socially awkward, I guess.

959
00:51:31,990 --> 00:51:35,910
the way I handled the whole Saria situation was pitiful.

960
00:51:36,710 --> 00:51:37,930
Absolutely pitiful.

961
00:51:43,510 --> 00:51:44,230
Okay.

962
00:51:44,330 --> 00:51:44,990
You're not impressed?

963
00:51:47,610 --> 00:51:48,710
She's crying.

964
00:51:54,660 --> 00:51:55,350
I am...

965
00:51:55,350 --> 00:51:56,590
Impa?!

966
00:51:58,060 --> 00:52:01,400
The old lady from Breath of the Wild?!

967
00:52:03,630 --> 00:52:06,310
I am Impa of the Sheikas.

968
00:52:06,590 --> 00:52:09,290
I am responsible for protecting Princess Zelda.

969
00:52:09,750 --> 00:52:12,270
Everything is exactly as the princess foretold.

970
00:52:12,710 --> 00:52:13,870
Holy shit!

971
00:52:15,430 --> 00:52:16,910
You are a courageous boy.

972
00:52:17,410 --> 00:52:19,570
You're heading out on a big new adventure, aren't you?

973
00:52:21,910 --> 00:52:25,930
My role in the princess's dream was to teach a melody to the one from the forest.

974
00:52:26,610 --> 00:52:27,050
Oh!

975
00:52:28,590 --> 00:52:29,410
You don't say!

976
00:52:32,260 --> 00:52:35,440
This is an ancient melody passed down by the royal family.

977
00:52:36,840 --> 00:52:40,800
I have played this song for Princess Zelda as a lullaby ever since she was a baby.

978
00:52:42,000 --> 00:52:44,640
There is mysterious power in these notes.

979
00:52:45,460 --> 00:52:47,160
Now listen carefully.

980
00:52:51,220 --> 00:52:52,180
Memorize this song.

981
00:53:17,530 --> 00:53:18,950
Oh, it's nice!

982
00:53:22,740 --> 00:53:24,120
It's ice!

983
00:53:25,780 --> 00:53:26,980
Like, whoa!

984
00:53:28,340 --> 00:53:30,520
You've learned Zelda's lullaby!

985
00:53:33,320 --> 00:53:36,480
If the castle soldiers find you, there will be trouble.

986
00:53:37,180 --> 00:53:38,700
Let me lead you out of the castle.

987
00:53:39,700 --> 00:53:40,420
No, no, no!

988
00:53:40,480 --> 00:53:42,280
I wanted to play the lullaby for Zelda.

989
00:53:43,760 --> 00:53:45,120
I wanted her to hear it.

990
00:53:50,920 --> 00:53:52,100
You brave lad!

991
00:53:52,420 --> 00:53:54,680
We must protect this beautiful land of Hyrule.

992
00:53:57,410 --> 00:53:59,010
Take a good look at that mountain.

993
00:53:59,810 --> 00:54:00,890
That is Death Mountain.

994
00:54:01,370 --> 00:54:02,570
Home of the Gorons.

995
00:54:03,350 --> 00:54:05,070
They hold the spiritual stone of fire.

996
00:54:06,210 --> 00:54:06,450
Aha!

997
00:54:09,310 --> 00:54:12,210
At the foot of Death Mountain, you will find my village.

998
00:54:12,890 --> 00:54:13,330
Kakariko!

999
00:54:14,110 --> 00:54:15,850
That is where I was born and raised.

1000
00:54:16,870 --> 00:54:17,310
Yes!

1001
00:54:17,510 --> 00:54:19,650
And that's where you will sit on a pillow later as an old lady.

1002
00:54:21,710 --> 00:54:22,670
Speaking in riddles.

1003
00:54:23,530 --> 00:54:26,470
You should talk to some of the villagers there before you go up Death Mountain.

1004
00:54:29,800 --> 00:54:32,740
The song I just taught you has some mysterious power.

1005
00:54:33,300 --> 00:54:35,820
Only royal family members are allowed to learn this song.

1006
00:54:37,180 --> 00:54:38,740
Wait, are you saying I'm part of the family?

1007
00:54:40,420 --> 00:54:43,540
Remember, it will help to prove your connection with the royal family.

1008
00:54:44,160 --> 00:54:44,960
Oh, okay.

1009
00:54:45,480 --> 00:54:46,000
It was confirmed.

1010
00:54:46,680 --> 00:54:49,540
The princess is waiting for you to return to the castle with the stones.

1011
00:54:50,240 --> 00:54:51,600
Alright, we're counting on you.

1012
00:54:52,000 --> 00:54:53,200
Don't worry, I got big stones.

1013
00:54:55,060 --> 00:54:56,160
I'm not afraid of anything.

1014
00:54:56,460 --> 00:54:56,860
Oh!

1015
00:54:57,820 --> 00:54:58,380
Wow.

1016
00:54:59,360 --> 00:55:00,560
What a magic trick.

1017
00:55:02,280 --> 00:55:04,200
I feel like that's something evil people do.

1018
00:55:04,820 --> 00:55:07,100
Normal people don't disappear like that.

1019
00:55:07,220 --> 00:55:09,500
That's just hella weird.

1020
00:55:10,140 --> 00:55:11,340
Let me see the map here.

1021
00:55:16,980 --> 00:55:19,720
Okay, so we actually have multiple...

1022
00:55:19,720 --> 00:55:21,120
Oh man, there's so many things.

1023
00:55:22,400 --> 00:55:23,300
Kakariko Village.

1024
00:55:24,280 --> 00:55:25,100
Death Mountain.

1025
00:55:25,880 --> 00:55:32,620
Wait a minute, they're even located kinda in, like, in the right spots, I mean.

1026
00:55:33,340 --> 00:55:36,200
I'm trying to think of the Breath of the Wild map right now.

1027
00:55:36,600 --> 00:55:40,560
Death Mountain is sort of northwest from Kakariko, if I'm not mistaken.

1028
00:55:42,820 --> 00:55:43,300
Market.

1029
00:55:43,300 --> 00:55:44,380
Lon Lon Ranch.

1030
00:55:47,060 --> 00:55:49,600
Dude, let's go back to the city real quick.

1031
00:55:49,780 --> 00:55:50,500
Also, yeah, save the game.

1032
00:55:50,580 --> 00:55:50,780
That's fine.

1033
00:55:54,990 --> 00:55:55,970
Let's go this way.

1034
00:56:05,740 --> 00:56:08,540
I'm gonna go play a little game now.

1035
00:56:09,060 --> 00:56:10,540
I have 25 coins.

1036
00:56:10,540 --> 00:56:11,640
I mean, rupees.

1037
00:56:12,840 --> 00:56:13,820
Also, check what I got.

1038
00:56:16,360 --> 00:56:17,220
What do you think about this?

1039
00:56:17,320 --> 00:56:17,680
Oh, wait, wait.

1040
00:56:18,120 --> 00:56:19,460
Someone here was a fan of Zelda, right?

1041
00:56:19,700 --> 00:56:19,960
You.

1042
00:56:22,970 --> 00:56:24,130
Oh man, nobody's impressed?

1043
00:56:25,330 --> 00:56:26,270
Look, I got a phone number.

1044
00:56:28,970 --> 00:56:30,990
Have you heard the legend of the Shadow Folk?

1045
00:56:31,490 --> 00:56:31,830
No.

1046
00:56:33,370 --> 00:56:34,450
They are the Sheikah.

1047
00:56:34,650 --> 00:56:36,050
The shadows of the Hylians.

1048
00:56:36,170 --> 00:56:36,950
Or Hylians, I mean.

1049
00:56:38,110 --> 00:56:41,990
They say they swore allegiance to the King of Hyrule and guarded the royal family.

1050
00:56:43,030 --> 00:56:44,270
Actually, it makes sense, I guess.

1051
00:56:44,990 --> 00:56:48,670
But with the long peace, no one has seen a Sheikah around here for a long time.

1052
00:56:49,110 --> 00:56:53,330
However, I heard there is one Sheikah woman living in the castle.

1053
00:56:54,610 --> 00:56:55,910
What a crazy coincidence!

1054
00:56:55,930 --> 00:56:57,110
I just spoke to her!

1055
00:57:00,060 --> 00:57:03,980
Do you know about the Temple of Time that we have in the northeast part of town?

1056
00:57:05,260 --> 00:57:08,900
Legends say that the Temple of Time is the entrance to the Sacred Realm.

1057
00:57:09,960 --> 00:57:11,400
Yeah, those legends are indeed true.

1058
00:57:12,120 --> 00:57:12,960
I did know that.

1059
00:57:13,060 --> 00:57:13,260
Thanks.

1060
00:57:14,740 --> 00:57:16,080
I just don't want to miss anything here.

1061
00:57:16,200 --> 00:57:16,740
So what about now?

1062
00:57:16,840 --> 00:57:17,220
Check this out.

1063
00:57:24,330 --> 00:57:25,170
Oh, wait, what?

1064
00:57:30,360 --> 00:57:32,780
Okay, I am pulling up the autograph.

1065
00:57:36,540 --> 00:57:36,940
Uh.

1066
00:57:43,750 --> 00:57:44,750
Oh, wait, what?

1067
00:57:52,920 --> 00:57:54,840
Okay, nobody's impressed by Zelda's Lullaby?

1068
00:57:56,680 --> 00:57:57,080
Really?

1069
00:57:58,560 --> 00:57:58,960
Alright.

1070
00:58:04,800 --> 00:58:09,020
Uh, there's a rumor going around that there is a potion shop that can make the ultimate medicine.

1071
00:58:09,360 --> 00:58:10,420
Yeah, you told me that.

1072
00:58:12,380 --> 00:58:14,320
Uh, I don't think I want to buy anything.

1073
00:58:15,960 --> 00:58:18,160
Where's that shop with, uh, with a little mini game?

1074
00:58:19,220 --> 00:58:19,980
Is it over here?

1075
00:58:20,180 --> 00:58:21,540
Watch me nail it first time now.

1076
00:58:25,040 --> 00:58:26,240
Oh, yeah, this is it.

1077
00:58:29,260 --> 00:58:29,940
This is it.

1078
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:30,380
Are you ready?

1079
00:58:32,420 --> 00:58:33,600
You want to play a game?

1080
00:58:34,360 --> 00:58:35,280
It's 20 rupees.

1081
00:58:35,980 --> 00:58:36,380
Yes.

1082
00:58:38,440 --> 00:58:41,540
Okay, now I need to remember the keybinds because they're apparently different when you're in here.

1083
00:58:42,240 --> 00:58:44,740
So shooting is, I think, uh, green.

1084
00:58:46,180 --> 00:58:47,940
Take aim at the targets from that platform.

1085
00:58:48,080 --> 00:58:48,400
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1086
00:58:50,060 --> 00:58:51,000
Draw your weapon with...

1087
00:58:51,000 --> 00:58:51,320
Okay, yeah.

1088
00:58:55,370 --> 00:58:56,030
Good.

1089
00:58:56,490 --> 00:58:57,570
Watch me nail it.

1090
00:58:58,730 --> 00:58:59,710
Oh my god.

1091
00:59:04,480 --> 00:59:05,900
Oh, that was so impossible.

1092
00:59:16,220 --> 00:59:16,780
No.

1093
00:59:17,580 --> 00:59:17,740
No.

1094
00:59:18,400 --> 00:59:18,600
No.

1095
00:59:19,180 --> 00:59:20,060
Too bad.

1096
00:59:21,160 --> 00:59:22,140
Practice hard and come back.

1097
00:59:24,200 --> 00:59:25,820
Uh, wait.

1098
00:59:27,460 --> 00:59:28,120
Yes.

1099
00:59:28,760 --> 00:59:29,360
Nope.

1100
00:59:29,640 --> 00:59:30,680
You don't have enough rupees.

1101
00:59:30,860 --> 00:59:31,160
Shit.

1102
00:59:31,160 --> 00:59:34,180
I thought I got enough to get a free retry.

1103
00:59:36,120 --> 00:59:36,600
Uh.

1104
00:59:38,180 --> 00:59:39,460
Hit Ada more, free retry.

1105
00:59:39,560 --> 00:59:39,840
Shit.

1106
00:59:41,520 --> 00:59:42,260
Okay, okay.

1107
00:59:42,380 --> 00:59:42,700
Fine.

1108
00:59:42,860 --> 00:59:43,260
Fine.

1109
00:59:43,500 --> 00:59:44,300
I'll be back later.

1110
00:59:44,640 --> 00:59:45,760
I'll be back later.

1111
00:59:46,720 --> 00:59:47,380
Oh well.

1112
00:59:47,600 --> 00:59:48,440
That went better.

1113
00:59:49,700 --> 00:59:50,840
Definitely better than last time.

1114
00:59:53,140 --> 00:59:54,600
Uh, what else do I need to do here?

1115
00:59:55,960 --> 00:59:56,820
Uh, I think I'm good.

1116
00:59:57,480 --> 00:59:58,860
Let's head to, uh, oh, wait.

1117
00:59:58,900 --> 01:00:00,460
I want to talk to a little girl once more.

1118
01:00:01,260 --> 01:00:02,760
Just to see if she has anything new to say.

1119
01:00:03,140 --> 01:00:05,160
And if not, then I'm going to go to Lon Lon Ranch.

1120
01:00:09,670 --> 01:00:10,490
Okay, she's gone.

1121
01:00:12,370 --> 01:00:12,950
She's gone.

1122
01:00:17,400 --> 01:00:18,960
Now we go into Lon Lon Ranch.

1123
01:00:25,780 --> 01:00:26,700
I want to get a horse.

1124
01:00:29,300 --> 01:00:29,960
Check what I got.

1125
01:00:32,540 --> 01:00:32,900
Ah.

1126
01:00:34,360 --> 01:00:35,340
Nobody likes the autograph.

1127
01:00:36,600 --> 01:00:38,620
I'm the only one as excited about this autograph.

1128
01:00:40,220 --> 01:00:40,900
Nobody cares.

1129
01:00:43,320 --> 01:00:44,680
Let's see if I remember the other song.

1130
01:00:45,340 --> 01:00:45,640
Uh.

1131
01:00:51,870 --> 01:00:53,210
It's so much easier to play now.

1132
01:00:55,450 --> 01:00:56,270
Buh, buh, buh.

1133
01:00:56,370 --> 01:00:57,690
Oh, I forgot the song now.

1134
01:00:58,150 --> 01:01:00,310
Da, da, da, da, da, da, da, da, da.

1135
01:01:01,190 --> 01:01:02,870
I need to go back there and listen to it.

1136
01:01:03,770 --> 01:01:04,250
But that's fine.

1137
01:01:05,310 --> 01:01:12,310
I do want to go back there today anyway because I need to, um, get the upgrade for my bandolier or whatever.

1138
01:01:12,590 --> 01:01:14,130
The thing that shoots rocks, you know?

1139
01:01:14,270 --> 01:01:15,030
Or little nuts.

1140
01:01:16,450 --> 01:01:17,430
Seats, I mean.

1141
01:01:19,390 --> 01:01:19,830
Oh.

1142
01:01:21,750 --> 01:01:24,910
What would Saria say if we told her we're going to save Hyrule?

1143
01:01:25,970 --> 01:01:27,890
She would totally fall into our arms.

1144
01:01:30,820 --> 01:01:32,560
Sounds like Navi's on my side here.

1145
01:01:32,800 --> 01:01:33,580
A real wingman.

1146
01:01:43,570 --> 01:01:44,390
Wait, there she is.

1147
01:01:45,310 --> 01:01:46,110
Next to the horse.

1148
01:01:50,750 --> 01:01:53,350
I'm going to check this out again and see if there's an evil voice in her again.

1149
01:01:56,460 --> 01:01:57,760
Oh my god, there he is.

1150
01:01:59,780 --> 01:02:00,180
Huh?

1151
01:02:01,440 --> 01:02:02,320
I'm awake already.

1152
01:02:03,020 --> 01:02:03,420
What?

1153
01:02:04,680 --> 01:02:05,760
Well, I'll be.

1154
01:02:06,220 --> 01:02:08,460
If it ain't the forest kid from the other day.

1155
01:02:09,100 --> 01:02:11,280
By the way, thanks a lot for waking me up.

1156
01:02:12,400 --> 01:02:15,780
It took some doing, but I finally got Malon back in a good mood.

1157
01:02:16,000 --> 01:02:16,360
Malon?

1158
01:02:16,520 --> 01:02:16,840
Malon?

1159
01:02:16,960 --> 01:02:18,120
I'm not sure how to pronounce that.

1160
01:02:19,220 --> 01:02:20,540
So, what are you up to today?

1161
01:02:21,160 --> 01:02:22,880
Got some free time on your hands, you say?

1162
01:02:22,880 --> 01:02:24,660
Well, how about a little game?

1163
01:02:25,360 --> 01:02:26,500
Does it involve money?

1164
01:02:27,300 --> 01:02:30,660
These three cuckoos I have here are special super cuckoos.

1165
01:02:31,680 --> 01:02:35,620
I'm going to throw these cuckoos into their gaggle of normal cuckoos.

1166
01:02:36,600 --> 01:02:43,020
If you can pick out these three special birds from among the normal cuckoos within the time limit, I'll give you something good.

1167
01:02:44,680 --> 01:02:46,260
If you can't find them, I win.

1168
01:02:46,860 --> 01:02:47,920
It'll be ten rupees.

1169
01:02:48,640 --> 01:02:48,980
Want to play?

1170
01:02:50,260 --> 01:02:50,700
Yes.

1171
01:02:51,620 --> 01:02:52,840
You don't have enough rupees.

1172
01:02:53,480 --> 01:02:53,920
Shit.

1173
01:02:56,060 --> 01:02:57,240
Man, I need that money.

1174
01:02:59,220 --> 01:03:01,240
What if I slay your cuckoos, huh?

1175
01:03:02,380 --> 01:03:03,180
What do you say then?

1176
01:03:04,360 --> 01:03:04,680
Qua.

1177
01:03:04,840 --> 01:03:05,080
Qua.

1178
01:03:06,860 --> 01:03:07,580
Excuse me.

1179
01:03:07,740 --> 01:03:08,840
I'm going to check up upstairs.

1180
01:03:12,580 --> 01:03:15,520
Everyone wants to play games for money in this world.

1181
01:03:24,220 --> 01:03:25,300
Can I sleep in your bed?

1182
01:03:34,460 --> 01:03:35,540
Yo, we just got money!

1183
01:03:37,140 --> 01:03:37,540
Ahoy!

1184
01:03:37,940 --> 01:03:38,820
We can play the game!

1185
01:03:41,000 --> 01:03:41,620
No way.

1186
01:03:41,660 --> 01:03:42,500
That was a lot of money too.

1187
01:03:42,680 --> 01:03:43,140
What the hell?

1188
01:03:46,210 --> 01:03:47,010
Okay, I'm ready.

1189
01:03:47,790 --> 01:03:48,190
Yes.

1190
01:03:49,430 --> 01:03:50,430
You have 30 seconds.

1191
01:03:50,870 --> 01:03:51,310
Alrighty then.

1192
01:03:51,430 --> 01:03:51,730
Get ready.

1193
01:03:52,350 --> 01:03:53,610
Here you go, the super cuckoos.

1194
01:03:54,470 --> 01:03:55,130
Start looking!

1195
01:03:57,950 --> 01:03:59,010
How would I know?

1196
01:04:05,080 --> 01:04:05,740
How do I know?

1197
01:04:10,210 --> 01:04:10,850
Who's super?

1198
01:04:14,180 --> 01:04:14,900
That's one of them.

1199
01:04:15,360 --> 01:04:16,100
Keep it up, keep it up!

1200
01:04:16,500 --> 01:04:17,060
Two more to find.

1201
01:04:17,220 --> 01:04:17,540
Oh shit.

1202
01:04:20,830 --> 01:04:21,230
Yes!

1203
01:04:21,710 --> 01:04:22,350
There's another.

1204
01:04:22,530 --> 01:04:23,070
Alright, now.

1205
01:04:23,410 --> 01:04:24,050
The moment of truth.

1206
01:04:24,310 --> 01:04:24,970
One more to find.

1207
01:04:31,620 --> 01:04:32,020
Golly!

1208
01:04:32,200 --> 01:04:33,240
I'll be darned!

1209
01:04:33,720 --> 01:04:34,780
It's plum incredible!

1210
01:04:36,020 --> 01:04:37,100
That's the last one!

1211
01:04:37,340 --> 01:04:38,360
You found them all!

1212
01:04:38,960 --> 01:04:39,620
Come on over here!

1213
01:04:40,240 --> 01:04:41,460
Dude, I'm a god gamer.

1214
01:04:43,640 --> 01:04:44,220
Hey you!

1215
01:04:44,740 --> 01:04:47,560
You've got the talent to be one of the world's best cowboys!

1216
01:04:49,100 --> 01:04:51,440
Uh, you know the word cow is in there, right?

1217
01:04:51,520 --> 01:04:52,400
This is not a chicken boy.

1218
01:04:54,240 --> 01:04:55,680
How would you like to marry Malon?

1219
01:04:56,000 --> 01:04:57,540
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

1220
01:04:59,980 --> 01:05:02,040
I'm sorry, but there's someone else.

1221
01:05:03,420 --> 01:05:04,000
Ha ha!

1222
01:05:04,180 --> 01:05:05,040
I was just kidding!

1223
01:05:05,420 --> 01:05:06,040
Just kidding!

1224
01:05:06,460 --> 01:05:08,140
I think you're a little young for that, aren't you?

1225
01:05:08,740 --> 01:05:09,320
Ha ha ha!

1226
01:05:10,140 --> 01:05:10,580
Oh!

1227
01:05:11,140 --> 01:05:15,380
I'm proud to present to you a simple, or sample, of our very own Lon Lon Milk!

1228
01:05:15,860 --> 01:05:17,780
You'll be energized the moment you drink it!

1229
01:05:18,320 --> 01:05:18,880
Oh yeah?

1230
01:05:19,160 --> 01:05:20,560
Let me guess, you've never had a taste.

1231
01:05:22,060 --> 01:05:23,220
You're sleeping all the time!

1232
01:05:23,980 --> 01:05:27,740
After you drink it, you can bring back the bottle and buy a refill anytime you want.

1233
01:05:28,800 --> 01:05:29,240
Really?

1234
01:05:30,840 --> 01:05:32,200
You've got Lon Lon Milk.

1235
01:05:32,540 --> 01:05:33,980
This milk is very nutritious.

1236
01:05:34,740 --> 01:05:37,180
Use it with C to recover your life energy.

1237
01:05:37,880 --> 01:05:38,320
Okay.

1238
01:05:39,320 --> 01:05:41,200
You will recover five hearts per drink.

1239
01:05:41,760 --> 01:05:43,240
There are two drinks per bottle.

1240
01:05:44,420 --> 01:05:45,380
It's like a potion.

1241
01:05:49,310 --> 01:05:50,010
Got it.

1242
01:05:52,350 --> 01:05:53,430
Oh yeah, listen to that.

1243
01:05:53,750 --> 01:05:55,190
That's definitely the evil laugh.

1244
01:05:57,270 --> 01:05:58,470
It's just cuckoos.

1245
01:06:03,000 --> 01:06:03,560
Money.

1246
01:06:07,920 --> 01:06:09,460
This guy is so drunk.

1247
01:06:11,100 --> 01:06:16,920
I can't believe that I, the great Ingo, am working on this dump of a ranch.

1248
01:06:18,120 --> 01:06:19,600
Because the owner is so lazy.

1249
01:06:19,900 --> 01:06:22,040
I always have to do all the work around here.

1250
01:06:23,360 --> 01:06:26,640
I, the hard working Ingo, should be in charge.

1251
01:06:26,960 --> 01:06:28,580
Not that lazy bum Talon.

1252
01:06:29,380 --> 01:06:31,300
I mean, I gotta be honest here.

1253
01:06:31,380 --> 01:06:32,160
He is kind of lazy.

1254
01:06:32,420 --> 01:06:33,520
He's just sleeping all day.

1255
01:06:38,470 --> 01:06:41,330
Dude, doesn't that move, sound like that meme?

1256
01:06:41,930 --> 01:06:44,030
The one that goes, uh, or something.

1257
01:06:44,870 --> 01:06:47,850
I don't know what the meme actually is, but, is this where it's from?

1258
01:06:50,250 --> 01:06:51,410
Can I interact with you?

1259
01:06:54,960 --> 01:06:57,120
Why is there a little interaction icon?

1260
01:07:00,780 --> 01:07:01,340
Huh.

1261
01:07:03,020 --> 01:07:04,220
Let me play you a song.

1262
01:07:18,460 --> 01:07:19,740
That's such a nice melody.

1263
01:07:21,220 --> 01:07:24,120
The cows do not care about the melody.

1264
01:07:26,480 --> 01:07:26,880
Okay.

1265
01:07:27,520 --> 01:07:28,260
Let's get out of here.

1266
01:07:40,980 --> 01:07:41,380
Malon!

1267
01:07:41,960 --> 01:07:42,920
Yeah, there you are.

1268
01:07:43,800 --> 01:07:45,380
I saw her in the distance before.

1269
01:07:47,340 --> 01:07:48,200
Hold on, I have an idea.

1270
01:07:51,560 --> 01:07:52,280
Okay, never mind.

1271
01:07:52,960 --> 01:07:53,120
Yo!

1272
01:07:59,810 --> 01:08:00,210
No!

1273
01:08:01,710 --> 01:08:02,110
Okay.

1274
01:08:02,930 --> 01:08:03,710
It was a test.

1275
01:08:06,870 --> 01:08:08,290
She likes to sing this song, huh?

1276
01:08:11,360 --> 01:08:11,800
Oh!

1277
01:08:12,100 --> 01:08:13,540
It's the fairy boy again.

1278
01:08:14,760 --> 01:08:16,080
I heard that you found my dad.

1279
01:08:16,660 --> 01:08:17,800
How did you like the castle?

1280
01:08:18,200 --> 01:08:19,060
Did you see the princess?

1281
01:08:19,440 --> 01:08:19,520
Hehe.

1282
01:08:20,880 --> 01:08:22,800
Dad came home in a hurry after you found him.

1283
01:08:24,000 --> 01:08:24,620
Oh, yeah?

1284
01:08:25,120 --> 01:08:25,780
Oh, yeah!

1285
01:08:26,040 --> 01:08:28,100
I have to introduce you to my friend, fairy boy.

1286
01:08:29,320 --> 01:08:30,160
She's this horse.

1287
01:08:30,380 --> 01:08:31,640
Her name is Epona.

1288
01:08:32,400 --> 01:08:33,260
Isn't she cute?

1289
01:08:36,320 --> 01:08:37,120
I guess so.

1290
01:08:37,180 --> 01:08:38,300
She's kind of small, though.

1291
01:08:40,420 --> 01:08:40,860
Hey!

1292
01:08:41,800 --> 01:08:42,280
Come here.

1293
01:08:42,560 --> 01:08:43,240
Let me ride you.

1294
01:08:45,520 --> 01:08:45,880
Yeah!

1295
01:08:54,660 --> 01:08:55,780
Oh my god, I almost hit her.

1296
01:08:56,620 --> 01:08:56,960
Sorry.

1297
01:08:58,260 --> 01:08:59,500
Let me play the song of my people.

1298
01:08:59,900 --> 01:09:01,580
I mean, when I say people, I mean Zelda.

1299
01:09:11,580 --> 01:09:12,220
Nobody cares.

1300
01:09:12,440 --> 01:09:13,180
What about the signature?

1301
01:09:13,340 --> 01:09:13,760
Check this out.

1302
01:09:13,840 --> 01:09:14,760
I have proof that I met her.

1303
01:09:18,840 --> 01:09:20,320
Looks like this item doesn't work here.

1304
01:09:20,520 --> 01:09:20,640
Okay.

1305
01:09:23,850 --> 01:09:24,210
Hmm.

1306
01:09:25,550 --> 01:09:27,210
Oh, we got some, uh...

1307
01:09:27,210 --> 01:09:28,350
Wait a minute.

1308
01:09:32,140 --> 01:09:33,940
She is singing a song as well.

1309
01:09:35,840 --> 01:09:37,800
Dude, we should try and replicate her song.

1310
01:09:42,330 --> 01:09:43,700
Be-be-be-be.

1311
01:09:45,410 --> 01:09:46,670
Be-be-be.

1312
01:09:48,370 --> 01:09:50,030
Uh, be-be-be.

1313
01:10:12,600 --> 01:10:13,260
Oh, wait.

1314
01:10:13,320 --> 01:10:13,420
No.

1315
01:10:13,660 --> 01:10:13,840
Uh.

1316
01:10:21,390 --> 01:10:22,050
That's it?

1317
01:10:23,910 --> 01:10:24,790
Did you like it?

1318
01:10:27,720 --> 01:10:30,380
It seems like Epona is afraid of you, fairy boy.

1319
01:10:31,700 --> 01:10:33,100
No, I'm not scary!

1320
01:10:33,360 --> 01:10:34,020
I mean, okay.

1321
01:10:34,220 --> 01:10:36,020
I guess I did try to shoot it with the...

1322
01:10:36,020 --> 01:10:37,880
With the hammock, but...

1323
01:10:37,880 --> 01:10:38,520
You know.

1324
01:10:39,700 --> 01:10:40,540
Hold on, let me listen.

1325
01:10:41,580 --> 01:10:41,980
Oh!

1326
01:10:42,160 --> 01:10:42,440
Oh!

1327
01:10:42,900 --> 01:10:45,840
Oh, hold on.

1328
01:10:46,640 --> 01:10:47,680
Oh, it's a long song!

1329
01:10:47,860 --> 01:10:48,000
Okay.

1330
01:10:48,220 --> 01:10:48,660
Long song.

1331
01:11:00,720 --> 01:11:01,400
Okay, okay.

1332
01:11:01,880 --> 01:11:02,580
I got it.

1333
01:11:03,660 --> 01:11:05,200
My mother composed this song.

1334
01:11:05,680 --> 01:11:06,380
Isn't it nice?

1335
01:11:06,720 --> 01:11:07,640
Let's sing together.

1336
01:11:08,560 --> 01:11:09,120
Yes!

1337
01:11:09,380 --> 01:11:09,680
Yes!

1338
01:11:09,960 --> 01:11:10,420
Let's do it!

1339
01:11:12,220 --> 01:11:12,740
Uh.

1340
01:11:15,180 --> 01:11:16,140
Oh, cute!

1341
01:11:16,160 --> 01:11:16,720
Ocarina!

1342
01:11:17,080 --> 01:11:18,940
Are you gonna play this song without Ocarina?

1343
01:11:20,060 --> 01:11:20,840
I am!

1344
01:11:21,420 --> 01:11:21,980
Oh!

1345
01:11:24,300 --> 01:11:25,720
You didn't need to tell me this.

1346
01:11:25,840 --> 01:11:26,580
I got it already.

1347
01:11:36,730 --> 01:11:37,290
Listen.

1348
01:11:38,150 --> 01:11:39,290
Fat-fingered, okay?

1349
01:11:51,310 --> 01:11:51,870
Nice!

1350
01:11:54,930 --> 01:11:56,430
You've learned Epona's song!

1351
01:12:00,340 --> 01:12:01,220
That's awesome!

1352
01:12:02,100 --> 01:12:03,340
Learning all the songs.

1353
01:12:03,560 --> 01:12:03,760
Cheers!

1354
01:12:08,800 --> 01:12:09,240
Oot!

1355
01:12:09,360 --> 01:12:09,600
Oot!

1356
01:12:09,940 --> 01:12:10,900
The owl is there!

1357
01:12:12,980 --> 01:12:14,140
Wait, you're not afraid of me anymore!

1358
01:12:16,620 --> 01:12:17,060
Epona!

1359
01:12:19,980 --> 01:12:20,940
Don't do it, Epona!

1360
01:12:34,560 --> 01:12:35,340
Are you happy now?

1361
01:12:36,460 --> 01:12:36,820
Hmm.

1362
01:12:39,240 --> 01:12:39,960
Oh, Epona!

1363
01:12:40,460 --> 01:12:42,100
She's grown fond of you, fairy boy!

1364
01:12:43,120 --> 01:12:43,800
Thank you!

1365
01:12:44,040 --> 01:12:45,460
I mean, that's nice.

1366
01:12:47,480 --> 01:12:48,880
Learning all the- Wait, hold on.

1367
01:12:49,000 --> 01:12:49,800
Is this gonna show up in here?

1368
01:12:50,920 --> 01:12:54,150
Oh, it is!

1369
01:12:54,250 --> 01:12:54,610
Look!

1370
01:12:57,050 --> 01:13:00,450
Okay, I was- I thought I had to memorize this stuff.

1371
01:13:00,590 --> 01:13:01,550
I mean, this is not that bad.

1372
01:13:01,550 --> 01:13:03,030
I-I could have memorized it, for sure.

1373
01:13:04,670 --> 01:13:05,290
Pretty cool.

1374
01:13:07,530 --> 01:13:09,630
We-we gotta pay attention to all the songs now.

1375
01:13:12,310 --> 01:13:13,850
Can I really not write any of these?

1376
01:13:18,240 --> 01:13:19,860
What if I play you the song here?

1377
01:13:21,100 --> 01:13:22,040
You're standing still.

1378
01:13:23,440 --> 01:13:23,840
Oh.

1379
01:13:25,220 --> 01:13:25,680
Thank you!

1380
01:13:35,940 --> 01:13:36,340
Okay.

1381
01:13:37,080 --> 01:13:37,440
All right.

1382
01:13:38,960 --> 01:13:40,340
There's gotta be some use for it.

1383
01:13:41,560 --> 01:13:43,180
Uh, let me check out this...

1384
01:13:43,180 --> 01:13:44,200
box over here.

1385
01:13:47,230 --> 01:13:48,630
