02:23:01,740 --> 02:23:02,740
Snorkel is what we need.

2499
02:23:19,240 --> 02:23:19,940
There we go.

2500
02:23:22,140 --> 02:23:22,580
Alright.

2501
02:23:23,840 --> 02:23:24,640
That was nice.

2502
02:23:27,480 --> 02:23:29,580
Wait a minute, I never went to see Saria.

2503
02:23:31,220 --> 02:23:32,820
Ah, it wasn't my intention anyway.

2504
02:23:33,240 --> 02:23:33,740
That's fine.

2505
02:23:34,180 --> 02:23:35,040
I'll see you later.

2506
02:23:37,040 --> 02:23:38,640
Nothing has changed here, I don't think.

2507
02:23:38,820 --> 02:23:40,040
Okay, let's just uh...

2508
02:23:40,040 --> 02:23:41,220
Let's go to where we need to go.

2509
02:23:41,920 --> 02:23:42,560
Main quest.

2510
02:23:44,680 --> 02:23:45,680
No more tarrying.

2511
02:23:55,180 --> 02:23:55,940
Hyrule field.

2512
02:23:57,060 --> 02:23:59,120
I am once again, on the warpath.

2513
02:23:59,680 --> 02:24:00,980
I gotta see the map here though.

2514
02:24:03,340 --> 02:24:04,960
Okay, I think I see an access point.

2515
02:24:05,540 --> 02:24:07,340
On the right, and the top right.

2516
02:24:07,920 --> 02:24:08,200
Kinda.

2517
02:24:08,860 --> 02:24:09,900
Let me try the right first.

2518
02:24:14,060 --> 02:24:15,680
I mean, the mountain's over there, we can see it!

2519
02:24:15,740 --> 02:24:15,920
Woah!

2520
02:24:18,680 --> 02:24:20,340
Why is there a child going...

2521
02:24:20,340 --> 02:24:21,060
Ooooooh!

2522
02:24:21,560 --> 02:24:22,340
When they wake up.

2523
02:24:23,100 --> 02:24:23,760
So weird.

2524
02:24:28,890 --> 02:24:29,290
Oh!

2525
02:24:29,370 --> 02:24:30,190
What's happening here?!

2526
02:24:32,350 --> 02:24:33,010
Na'vi?

2527
02:24:36,210 --> 02:24:37,470
Na'vi just gave me a hint.

2528
02:24:37,950 --> 02:24:38,470
Look!

2529
02:24:39,010 --> 02:24:40,130
It's pointing to here.

2530
02:24:47,500 --> 02:24:48,340
Nothing down there?

2531
02:24:56,170 --> 02:24:57,570
Just gonna follow the edge here.

2532
02:24:58,750 --> 02:24:59,850
Oh wait, we got something.

2533
02:25:00,830 --> 02:25:01,350
Ooooooh!

2534
02:25:01,430 --> 02:25:02,650
What is this?!

2535
02:25:02,650 --> 02:25:03,410
Oh god!

2536
02:25:06,010 --> 02:25:06,790
Stay away!

2537
02:25:07,670 --> 02:25:08,710
Foul machinations.

2538
02:25:11,670 --> 02:25:12,430
Sora's river!

2539
02:25:12,430 --> 02:25:15,350
Watch out for swift current and strong undertow.

2540
02:25:16,530 --> 02:25:17,310
Sora's domain!

2541
02:25:18,990 --> 02:25:20,190
Alright, let's not hit that way.

2542
02:25:20,950 --> 02:25:22,150
We have a quest up here.

2543
02:25:27,390 --> 02:25:28,770
Man, you guys have pushovers.

2544
02:25:29,910 --> 02:25:32,530
When is this game gonna present a real challenge, eh?

2545
02:25:32,970 --> 02:25:35,050
The god gamer hasn't died once yet.

2546
02:25:36,410 --> 02:25:37,590
Just putting it out there.

2547
02:25:40,500 --> 02:25:41,720
Can I jump across this?

2548
02:25:43,300 --> 02:25:44,040
Oh, hell yeah!

2549
02:25:50,590 --> 02:25:51,610
Something hiding down here.

2550
02:25:57,030 --> 02:25:58,270
What a nice bridge over there.

2551
02:26:01,210 --> 02:26:03,090
So I think we're on the path now.

2552
02:26:03,330 --> 02:26:04,350
Over here there should be something.

2553
02:26:04,810 --> 02:26:05,330
Or is it here?

2554
02:26:05,410 --> 02:26:05,930
Oh, there it is!

2555
02:26:10,930 --> 02:26:11,690
Kakariko Village!

2556
02:26:12,050 --> 02:26:13,670
Death Mountain Trail starting point.

2557
02:26:14,030 --> 02:26:14,730
Let's do it!

2558
02:26:17,110 --> 02:26:18,370
Let's check it out.

2559
02:26:19,150 --> 02:26:19,750
Let's

2560
02:26:31,650 --> 02:26:31,650
check it out.

2561
02:26:31,650 --> 02:26:32,770
Here we are!

2562
02:26:34,510 --> 02:26:35,670
Ding dong!

2563
02:26:35,910 --> 02:26:36,350
Ding dong!

2564
02:26:36,790 --> 02:26:39,090
I'm a clock soldier of Kakariko.

2565
02:26:39,530 --> 02:26:41,630
The current time is 0841.

2566
02:26:43,450 --> 02:26:44,890
Hello there, son.

2567
02:26:45,570 --> 02:26:47,570
Tell this attendant, the great Impa.

2568
02:26:47,910 --> 02:26:50,050
Open this village to the common people.

2569
02:26:50,850 --> 02:26:57,370
We have only a small population now, but someday this place will be as lively as Hyrule Castle Town.

2570
02:26:57,650 --> 02:26:58,870
Oh, yes it will.

2571
02:27:00,210 --> 02:27:05,570
Climb up the stairs at the north end of the village to find the trail that leads up Death Mountain.

2572
02:27:06,970 --> 02:27:10,530
But you need the king's permission to actually go up the mountain.

2573
02:27:11,630 --> 02:27:12,270
Thanks, dude.

2574
02:27:14,390 --> 02:27:15,690
Looks like you need some milk.

2575
02:27:16,330 --> 02:27:17,310
Give you that energy.

2576
02:27:19,390 --> 02:27:20,150
Who are you?

2577
02:27:23,330 --> 02:27:29,430
I am the boss of the carpenters that Impa hired to improve this village and make it into a true city.

2578
02:27:30,070 --> 02:27:32,930
Wait a minute, are you guys the Bolson Construction Company?

2579
02:27:34,670 --> 02:27:37,170
But young men these days don't have any ambition.

2580
02:27:37,770 --> 02:27:38,870
You know what I mean, kid?

2581
02:27:40,210 --> 02:27:40,690
No.

2582
02:27:40,690 --> 02:27:45,750
My workers are just running aimlessly around the village and they're not making any progress at all.

2583
02:27:46,790 --> 02:27:48,870
Even my own son doesn't have a job.

2584
02:27:49,070 --> 02:27:50,830
And he just wanders around all day.

2585
02:27:52,070 --> 02:27:53,710
They're all worthless, I tell ya.

2586
02:27:54,790 --> 02:27:55,430
Oh, yeah?

2587
02:27:56,010 --> 02:27:57,310
You should whip them into shape.

2588
02:27:59,690 --> 02:28:00,690
Maybe I should do it.

2589
02:28:02,190 --> 02:28:03,110
Is that you?

2590
02:28:03,250 --> 02:28:03,970
Are you one of the sons?

2591
02:28:05,270 --> 02:28:06,350
Excuse me, son.

2592
02:28:09,640 --> 02:28:13,300
All day long we are working on many construction projects in the village.

2593
02:28:13,800 --> 02:28:15,980
It's gonna take a while before everything is done.

2594
02:28:16,760 --> 02:28:18,700
Our boss works us very hard.

2595
02:28:20,700 --> 02:28:22,000
Why do I not believe you?

2596
02:28:24,480 --> 02:28:25,820
Why are you running like that?

2597
02:28:27,760 --> 02:28:29,480
Dark, narrow, scary.

2598
02:28:30,260 --> 02:28:31,840
Well of three features.

2599
02:28:33,840 --> 02:28:34,480
Uh-huh.

2600
02:28:35,980 --> 02:28:36,820
I'm going in.

2601
02:28:40,620 --> 02:28:42,120
It's actually just a well.

2602
02:28:48,440 --> 02:28:50,320
Okay, yeah, we need to be able to dive more.

2603
02:28:51,880 --> 02:28:52,920
A scuba mask.

2604
02:28:56,570 --> 02:28:57,730
We got cuckoos.

2605
02:29:04,730 --> 02:29:06,430
I see a guy running up on a beam.

2606
02:29:07,610 --> 02:29:08,430
He's slacking.

2607
02:29:12,090 --> 02:29:13,050
Excuse me, sir.

2608
02:29:15,750 --> 02:29:16,670
No, no, no, no.

2609
02:29:16,730 --> 02:29:17,430
Link, what are you doing?

2610
02:29:18,790 --> 02:29:19,590
Come on now.

2611
02:29:23,930 --> 02:29:24,850
Up you go.

2612
02:29:25,370 --> 02:29:26,230
Now slowly.

2613
02:29:31,810 --> 02:29:32,690
There we go.

2614
02:29:36,270 --> 02:29:37,150
There we are.

2615
02:29:39,370 --> 02:29:39,890
Sir!

2616
02:29:40,670 --> 02:29:42,530
Look at that poor girl over there.

2617
02:29:42,770 --> 02:29:45,230
She works so hard taking care of her chickens.

2618
02:29:45,670 --> 02:29:47,490
Even though touching them gives her goose bumps.

2619
02:29:48,690 --> 02:29:49,910
I love bumping geese.

2620
02:29:50,490 --> 02:29:51,190
What a trooper.

2621
02:29:51,430 --> 02:29:52,850
I would really like to help her.

2622
02:29:53,110 --> 02:29:55,350
I've just been feeling so charitable these days.

2623
02:29:55,770 --> 02:29:56,870
Don't you feel that way too?

2624
02:29:57,690 --> 02:29:58,710
Uh, maybe.

2625
02:29:59,130 --> 02:30:01,070
Oh, you asshole almost pushed me down.

2626
02:30:01,250 --> 02:30:02,150
That was not very charitable.

2627
02:30:04,950 --> 02:30:06,250
What a jump.

2628
02:30:08,830 --> 02:30:10,250
Oh, that's the girl down there.

2629
02:30:10,950 --> 02:30:11,770
Hello there.

2630
02:30:13,070 --> 02:30:13,610
M'lady?

2631
02:30:17,630 --> 02:30:18,570
You're distraught.

2632
02:30:20,630 --> 02:30:21,790
What should I do?

2633
02:30:22,150 --> 02:30:23,950
My cuckoos have all flown away.

2634
02:30:24,650 --> 02:30:26,330
Wait, this is a story I'm familiar with.

2635
02:30:27,130 --> 02:30:28,210
You little boy, please.

2636
02:30:28,750 --> 02:30:30,710
Please help me bring them back to this pen.

2637
02:30:31,690 --> 02:30:33,330
This is very familiar.

2638
02:30:35,430 --> 02:30:36,330
Come here, you.

2639
02:30:38,450 --> 02:30:39,130
In you go.

2640
02:30:40,210 --> 02:30:41,190
Oh, heck yeah.

2641
02:30:43,290 --> 02:30:44,810
Oh, it's going nuts in there.

2642
02:30:47,110 --> 02:30:48,250
I see a cuckoo.

2643
02:30:49,290 --> 02:30:50,050
Watch this.

2644
02:30:50,590 --> 02:30:51,030
Aw.

2645
02:30:51,510 --> 02:30:53,170
I was about to do some MLG gaming.

2646
02:30:55,250 --> 02:30:56,890
Wait, how do I actually get up there?

2647
02:31:01,030 --> 02:31:01,890
Mysteries abound.

2648
02:31:06,400 --> 02:31:08,240
If I go on the roof, I can jump down.

2649
02:31:10,080 --> 02:31:11,400
That could be a possibility.

2650
02:31:13,260 --> 02:31:13,860
What's that?

2651
02:31:15,860 --> 02:31:16,300
Insects.

2652
02:31:17,280 --> 02:31:17,720
Yuck.

2653
02:31:22,890 --> 02:31:24,270
Navi, now's the time to tell me.

2654
02:31:26,960 --> 02:31:28,140
Oh, we got another guard.

2655
02:31:29,460 --> 02:31:30,480
Check this out, you mad.

2656
02:31:31,080 --> 02:31:31,700
Oh, yeah.

2657
02:31:35,290 --> 02:31:36,170
Nice music here.

2658
02:31:36,990 --> 02:31:38,750
This used to be the great Impa's house.

2659
02:31:39,210 --> 02:31:40,910
But she doesn't live here any longer.

2660
02:31:41,770 --> 02:31:43,590
It is now open to all villagers.

2661
02:31:44,190 --> 02:31:44,990
You're free to go on in.

2662
02:31:46,190 --> 02:31:48,350
This village used to be a Sheikah village.

2663
02:31:48,610 --> 02:31:50,510
The great Impa opened it to everyone.

2664
02:31:51,370 --> 02:31:55,090
That does sound like something the greatest of Impas would do.

2665
02:31:57,450 --> 02:31:57,970
Okay.

2666
02:31:58,370 --> 02:31:59,010
I'm going in.

2667
02:32:04,590 --> 02:32:05,550
What are y'all cooking?

2668
02:32:07,390 --> 02:32:09,830
Is that a picture of a sword inside a bear?

2669
02:32:10,230 --> 02:32:11,230
What is that?

2670
02:32:13,370 --> 02:32:14,650
Like a dead bear.

2671
02:32:19,040 --> 02:32:19,500
Oh!

2672
02:32:21,860 --> 02:32:22,600
Hey, cow!

2673
02:32:23,140 --> 02:32:24,340
Look what I got for you.

2674
02:32:33,950 --> 02:32:35,710
Uh, yeah, let's talk to Zaria.

2675
02:32:37,350 --> 02:32:37,790
Link?

2676
02:32:38,190 --> 02:32:39,630
This is Zaria, can you hear me?

2677
02:32:40,690 --> 02:32:42,590
The forest is connected to many places.

2678
02:32:42,930 --> 02:32:46,270
If you can hear my song, you must be somewhere that is connected to the forest.

2679
02:32:47,250 --> 02:32:47,690
Awesome.

2680
02:32:48,350 --> 02:32:49,570
Wanna talk to Zaria again?

2681
02:32:50,830 --> 02:32:52,250
Will that ever do anything new?

2682
02:32:52,910 --> 02:32:53,350
Or...

2683
02:32:53,350 --> 02:32:54,210
Okay, it's not.

2684
02:32:54,930 --> 02:32:55,730
Uh, I'm good.

2685
02:32:55,870 --> 02:32:56,190
Thanks.

2686
02:32:57,290 --> 02:32:58,970
That was actually not the song I wanted to play.

2687
02:33:00,010 --> 02:33:00,750
Let me try again.

2688
02:33:06,110 --> 02:33:07,390
I forgot the songs.

2689
02:33:08,570 --> 02:33:09,770
Good thing I have a reminder.

2690
02:33:13,550 --> 02:33:14,330
Epona song.

2691
02:33:17,630 --> 02:33:18,070
Okay.

2692
02:33:18,070 --> 02:33:18,850
Tut tut tut tut tut tut tut.

2693
02:33:18,970 --> 02:33:19,150
Okay.

2694
02:33:29,290 --> 02:33:29,950
Open up.

2695
02:33:32,590 --> 02:33:33,010
Moooo!

2696
02:33:34,750 --> 02:33:35,970
What a nice song!

2697
02:33:36,430 --> 02:33:37,930
It reminds me of the pasture.

2698
02:33:38,910 --> 02:33:41,730
That song makes me feel so good I can produce a lot of milk.

2699
02:33:42,490 --> 02:33:43,450
Oh, that's too bad.

2700
02:33:43,610 --> 02:33:46,770
If you had something to put it in, I could give you some... to you.

2701
02:33:47,210 --> 02:33:47,890
Wait, I do!

2702
02:33:49,010 --> 02:33:49,650
What do you mean?

2703
02:33:49,770 --> 02:33:50,470
It's half full!

2704
02:33:51,250 --> 02:33:53,470
I thought maybe you would open this pen for me, but...

2705
02:33:54,130 --> 02:33:55,350
Okay, what about the other song?

2706
02:33:55,470 --> 02:33:56,010
Sell the song.

2707
02:33:57,090 --> 02:33:57,570
Tut tut tut.

2708
02:34:11,280 --> 02:34:12,920
Okay, no response from you, huh?

2709
02:34:14,100 --> 02:34:14,500
Okay.

2710
02:34:16,380 --> 02:34:17,300
Wanna play it rough?

2711
02:34:21,140 --> 02:34:22,400
Oh, there's a guy down there!

2712
02:34:22,520 --> 02:34:23,200
I didn't even see him!

2713
02:34:24,760 --> 02:34:25,300
Wait, what?

2714
02:34:27,100 --> 02:34:28,900
Did I just steal from underneath his pillow?

2715
02:34:29,460 --> 02:34:30,140
That's mean.

2716
02:34:32,640 --> 02:34:33,940
Oh no, there's a chest up there!

2717
02:34:34,040 --> 02:34:34,500
How do I get it?

2718
02:34:39,850 --> 02:34:40,630
Ah, dammit.

2719
02:34:40,810 --> 02:34:40,890
Okay.

2720
02:34:41,150 --> 02:34:41,350
You!

2721
02:34:43,250 --> 02:34:43,910
Hey kid!

2722
02:34:44,230 --> 02:34:46,550
Do you always enter other people's houses without permission?

2723
02:34:47,390 --> 02:34:48,910
Didn't your parents teach you any manners?

2724
02:34:49,430 --> 02:34:49,690
No!

2725
02:34:49,850 --> 02:34:50,710
I'm from the forest.

2726
02:34:50,890 --> 02:34:51,710
I'm a fairy boy.

2727
02:34:52,770 --> 02:34:53,610
Oh, well.

2728
02:34:54,810 --> 02:34:56,530
Did you see a lady behind this house?

2729
02:34:56,930 --> 02:34:58,250
She's going through hard times.

2730
02:34:58,970 --> 02:34:59,690
Yeah, I did.

2731
02:35:00,270 --> 02:35:00,930
Oh well.

2732
02:35:01,990 --> 02:35:05,210
If that lady asks you about chickens, you should listen to her.

2733
02:35:06,470 --> 02:35:06,870
Okay!

2734
02:35:07,330 --> 02:35:07,950
I will.

2735
02:35:08,990 --> 02:35:10,050
I mean, I already did.

2736
02:35:10,770 --> 02:35:11,870
And you mean cuckoos, right?

2737
02:35:12,090 --> 02:35:12,750
Not chickens.

2738
02:35:16,060 --> 02:35:17,020
Get it right, man.

2739
02:35:21,220 --> 02:35:22,540
Maybe I can jump to this roof.

2740
02:35:22,900 --> 02:35:24,040
If I'm good enough.

2741
02:35:24,280 --> 02:35:25,340
No, no way, no way.

2742
02:35:27,980 --> 02:35:28,380
Hmm.

2743
02:35:28,720 --> 02:35:29,680
How do I get in here?

2744
02:35:32,200 --> 02:35:34,100
Maybe by a skill jump here.

2745
02:35:36,620 --> 02:35:37,380
Actually, wait a minute.

2746
02:35:37,500 --> 02:35:38,300
That seems doable.

2747
02:35:40,400 --> 02:35:41,460
Let me remove this shield.

2748
02:35:43,620 --> 02:35:44,180
Watch this.

2749
02:35:44,360 --> 02:35:44,600
You ready?

2750
02:35:49,470 --> 02:35:49,770
Duh!

2751
02:35:50,510 --> 02:35:50,950
Hold on.

2752
02:35:51,150 --> 02:35:53,110
That was not entirely intended.

2753
02:35:55,190 --> 02:35:55,790
Oh, man!

2754
02:35:55,970 --> 02:35:56,530
That was so close.

2755
02:35:59,940 --> 02:36:02,380
This is probably not the right way to do this, but, you know...

2756
02:36:02,380 --> 02:36:03,440
Nah, I don't think so.

2757
02:36:04,000 --> 02:36:05,580
Maybe you can get one of these guys to give me a boost.

2758
02:36:06,340 --> 02:36:06,940
Hey, sir!

2759
02:36:10,650 --> 02:36:11,030
Okay.

2760
02:36:11,350 --> 02:36:12,150
Can I jump on you?

2761
02:36:13,350 --> 02:36:14,410
Oh, that's not gonna...

2762
02:36:14,410 --> 02:36:14,870
Of course.

2763
02:36:17,510 --> 02:36:22,370
Maybe one of these guys will, you know, run past here and I can somehow jump on their head.

2764
02:36:24,770 --> 02:36:25,610
What's going on up here?

2765
02:36:33,190 --> 02:36:34,070
What do we got, eh?

2766
02:36:34,710 --> 02:36:36,550
They got scaffolding permits here too, I see.

2767
02:36:42,380 --> 02:36:43,560
Oh, another cuckoo!

2768
02:36:44,300 --> 02:36:45,320
I gotta bring it back.

2769
02:36:46,160 --> 02:36:47,840
My little boy isn't here right now.

2770
02:36:48,280 --> 02:36:50,120
I think he went to play in the graveyard.

2771
02:36:50,800 --> 02:36:51,100
Ooh.

2772
02:36:52,740 --> 02:36:53,420
That's not good.

2773
02:36:55,000 --> 02:36:56,420
What do you mean play in the graveyard?

2774
02:36:58,300 --> 02:36:58,680
Sir!

2775
02:36:59,460 --> 02:37:02,280
A job where you can make a lot of money without much effort?

2776
02:37:02,480 --> 02:37:02,820
Haha!

2777
02:37:03,020 --> 02:37:04,880
The only thing I can think of is thievery!

2778
02:37:05,380 --> 02:37:06,380
Is that a bad idea?

2779
02:37:08,060 --> 02:37:11,520
You know, I wouldn't know anything about it, because I have never stolen a rupee in my life.

2780
02:37:13,180 --> 02:37:14,580
That is not something I would do.

2781
02:37:16,800 --> 02:37:17,880
I'll just bring you back, eh?

2782
02:37:20,720 --> 02:37:21,120
Oh!

2783
02:37:22,500 --> 02:37:24,240
Oh, it's just... oh, I get it now.

2784
02:37:24,480 --> 02:37:26,420
It's just like, uh, Breath of the Wild!

2785
02:37:33,610 --> 02:37:34,010
Yeah!

2786
02:37:37,480 --> 02:37:38,480
There we go!

2787
02:37:43,490 --> 02:37:44,950
Now, of course, this game is old.

2788
02:37:45,830 --> 02:37:47,550
So, it's more like the other game...

2789
02:37:50,450 --> 02:37:51,950
used some nostalgia, I guess.

2790
02:37:54,970 --> 02:37:56,950
I'm kinda sad a lot of that went over my head, you know?

2791
02:37:57,030 --> 02:38:00,590
Like, when I played Breath of the Wild, I didn't realize a lot of this stuff came from...

2792
02:38:00,970 --> 02:38:01,830
the older games.

2793
02:38:03,110 --> 02:38:05,110
Well, of course it did, to some degree, but...

2794
02:38:05,790 --> 02:38:06,350
Is that all?

2795
02:38:08,070 --> 02:38:09,570
My cuckoos have run away!

2796
02:38:09,870 --> 02:38:10,930
I... I got them, though.

2797
02:38:12,110 --> 02:38:13,310
Okay, there's more, I guess.

2798
02:38:14,110 --> 02:38:15,370
Wait, so this guy's running up here.

2799
02:38:18,390 --> 02:38:19,030
What's this?

2800
02:38:20,410 --> 02:38:21,610
Kakariko Village Graveyard.

2801
02:38:21,850 --> 02:38:22,070
Okay.

2802
02:38:23,370 --> 02:38:24,050
Excuse me!

2803
02:38:25,430 --> 02:38:27,710
I'm gonna go look for this child, playing in the graveyard.

2804
02:38:28,630 --> 02:38:29,630
That doesn't seem good.

2805
02:38:34,810 --> 02:38:36,350
That looks like a zombie child.

2806
02:38:39,860 --> 02:38:41,800
Heart-pounding grave-digging tour.

2807
02:38:42,400 --> 02:38:44,240
From 18 to 21 Hyrule time.

2808
02:38:44,960 --> 02:38:46,180
Dampe, the gravekeeper.

2809
02:38:46,780 --> 02:38:47,860
Wait, what time is it?

2810
02:39:00,830 --> 02:39:01,710
What's this?

2811
02:39:02,730 --> 02:39:03,370
Bugs.

2812
02:39:03,930 --> 02:39:04,470
Money.

2813
02:39:05,870 --> 02:39:06,770
And bunny.

2814
02:39:07,050 --> 02:39:07,630
Bugs Bunny!

2815
02:39:12,230 --> 02:39:13,290
Rest in peace.

2816
02:39:13,690 --> 02:39:17,810
Here lie the souls of those who swore fealty to the royal family of Hyrule.

2817
02:39:18,650 --> 02:39:22,810
The Sheikah, guardians of the royal family and founders of Kakariko.

2818
02:39:23,450 --> 02:39:25,870
Watch over these spirits in their eternal slumber.

2819
02:39:33,720 --> 02:39:34,600
That's an oven!

2820
02:39:38,480 --> 02:39:39,640
Be quiet!

2821
02:39:40,580 --> 02:39:42,000
It's only 8.41.

2822
02:39:42,860 --> 02:39:46,340
I, Dampe, the gravekeeper, am in bed now.

2823
02:39:47,240 --> 02:39:48,540
Go away and play!

2824
02:39:49,060 --> 02:39:50,720
Maybe you can find a ghost in the daytime?

2825
02:39:53,420 --> 02:39:54,180
Sorry, what?

2826
02:39:55,620 --> 02:39:56,640
Okay, sorry.

2827
02:39:58,780 --> 02:40:00,060
I guess I'll come back.

2828
02:40:01,280 --> 02:40:02,320
Now you...

2829
02:40:03,240 --> 02:40:04,540
You look sick.

2830
02:40:05,060 --> 02:40:06,860
Like you're suffering from a sickness.

2831
02:40:07,760 --> 02:40:12,740
Little kids can't go on the heart-pounding grave-digging tour described on the sign.

2832
02:40:13,680 --> 02:40:18,220
Since I can't do that, I'm just imitating Dampe, the gravekeeper, all day.

2833
02:40:19,120 --> 02:40:22,720
But with my cute face, I'm not heart-pounding at all, am I?

2834
02:40:23,460 --> 02:40:24,240
I don't know.

2835
02:40:24,440 --> 02:40:24,680
I don't know.

2836
02:40:24,680 --> 02:40:25,720
He sounded German to me, certainly.

2837
02:40:26,980 --> 02:40:28,180
Who's resting here?

2838
02:40:29,560 --> 02:40:30,720
Oh, Navi!

2839
02:40:31,760 --> 02:40:33,720
Impa said that the spiritual stone...

2840
02:40:33,720 --> 02:40:34,280
Navi!

2841
02:40:34,720 --> 02:40:35,320
Navi!

2842
02:40:35,640 --> 02:40:36,640
Listen, I'm...

2843
02:40:36,640 --> 02:40:37,600
I'm on my way there.

2844
02:40:37,980 --> 02:40:38,580
Okay?

2845
02:40:39,280 --> 02:40:40,000
Calm yourself.

2846
02:40:44,370 --> 02:40:45,890
Maybe I read it from the other side.

2847
02:40:47,170 --> 02:40:47,770
No?

2848
02:40:58,990 --> 02:41:00,770
I wanna read about these dead people.

2849
02:41:01,070 --> 02:41:01,830
Is that weird?

2850
02:41:09,400 --> 02:41:10,440
Oh, it's raining.

2851
02:41:12,400 --> 02:41:13,680
Actually kind of a vibe.

2852
02:41:16,180 --> 02:41:17,560
Royal Family's Tomb.

2853
02:41:18,500 --> 02:41:19,300
Ooh, really?

2854
02:41:19,680 --> 02:41:20,860
They're buried here.

2855
02:41:34,170 --> 02:41:35,030
Uh-oh!

2856
02:41:35,350 --> 02:41:37,390
Don't cause trouble, I'll tell Dampe.

2857
02:41:42,450 --> 02:41:42,830
Okay.

2858
02:41:42,830 --> 02:41:44,070
Oh, oh, okay, sorry.

2859
02:41:44,850 --> 02:41:46,630
I'm gonna go on the other side where you can't see me.

2860
02:41:49,210 --> 02:41:49,590
Little...

2861
02:41:49,590 --> 02:41:50,910
Uh, what do you call it?

2862
02:41:52,010 --> 02:41:53,330
Someone who tells tales.

2863
02:41:56,070 --> 02:41:56,450
Snitch!

2864
02:41:57,370 --> 02:41:58,430
You damn snitch!

2865
02:41:59,390 --> 02:42:00,990
Come on, let me do my thing.

2866
02:42:03,650 --> 02:42:04,410
Little kids...

2867
02:42:04,410 --> 02:42:05,290
Yeah, yeah, yeah, shut up, kid.

2868
02:42:11,540 --> 02:42:13,420
I guess I'll come back at some other time.

2869
02:42:14,440 --> 02:42:15,420
Wait a minute, this one is green.

2870
02:42:15,540 --> 02:42:16,400
Let me... let me try this one.

2871
02:42:20,240 --> 02:42:20,600
Hmm...

2872
02:42:20,600 --> 02:42:22,320
Someone special is resting here.

2873
02:42:24,260 --> 02:42:25,000
Something tells me...

2874
02:42:25,000 --> 02:42:27,120
I don't know what it is, but there's something about this gravestone.

2875
02:42:28,220 --> 02:42:29,420
That just speaks to me, you know?

2876
02:42:33,260 --> 02:42:33,620
Okay.

2877
02:42:33,900 --> 02:42:35,340
I guess time doesn't move while we're in here.

2878
02:42:36,540 --> 02:42:37,440
18 and 21.

2879
02:42:38,800 --> 02:42:39,640
Let's keep that in mind.

2880
02:42:43,970 --> 02:42:45,350
Uh, let's find the cuckoos.

2881
02:42:49,910 --> 02:42:50,910
I see a ladder.

2882
02:42:51,110 --> 02:42:51,610
Oh, a door.

2883
02:42:52,790 --> 02:42:53,650
Who lives here?

2884
02:42:54,930 --> 02:42:55,870
The Millerman?

2885
02:42:56,250 --> 02:42:57,030
Question mark.

2886
02:42:58,310 --> 02:43:00,490
Yo, this is giving me Super Mario 64 vibes.

2887
02:43:14,470 --> 02:43:16,590
Holy shit, this song is amazing!

2888
02:43:23,240 --> 02:43:24,480
What a banger!

2889
02:43:32,500 --> 02:43:33,440
I am enchanted!

2890
02:43:34,580 --> 02:43:35,140
Go

2891
02:43:38,690 --> 02:43:39,250
around!

2892
02:43:39,490 --> 02:43:41,150
Go around and around and around!

2893
02:43:41,150 --> 02:43:41,990
What fun!

2894
02:43:42,270 --> 02:43:43,370
I'm so happy!

2895
02:43:44,690 --> 02:43:47,710
I'm a music man who loves to go around and around!

2896
02:43:48,170 --> 02:43:49,290
Go around and around!

2897
02:43:50,650 --> 02:43:54,290
I'm trying to come up with a musical theme inspired by this windmill.

2898
02:43:54,530 --> 02:43:56,470
Going around and around and around?

2899
02:43:57,410 --> 02:43:58,990
Dude, you are killing it!

2900
02:44:00,070 --> 02:44:01,150
You're doing it!

2901
02:44:01,150 --> 02:44:01,170
Guys!

2902
02:44:03,640 --> 02:44:06,340
Do, do, do, do, do, do, do.

2903
02:44:07,920 --> 02:44:08,920
Holy crap, dude!

2904
02:44:09,060 --> 02:44:09,560
This is incredible!

2905
02:44:11,340 --> 02:44:12,940
I'm going to go around and around and around!

2906
02:44:15,580 --> 02:44:16,340
Something will happen.

2907
02:44:20,240 --> 02:44:21,380
I'm starting to feel sick!

2908
02:44:23,060 --> 02:44:23,640
Oh no!

2909
02:44:28,020 --> 02:44:28,520
I'm back!

2910
02:44:28,900 --> 02:44:29,780
Let me try the other way.

2911
02:44:37,090 --> 02:44:38,050
Come on, come on, come on!

2912
02:44:38,050 --> 02:44:38,890
Something's gotta happen.

2913
02:44:41,050 --> 02:44:43,470
Oh man, this is the best song in the game so far.

2914
02:44:45,730 --> 02:44:47,510
They really outdid themselves here.

2915
02:44:48,050 --> 02:44:50,110
This is even better than The Last Woods.

2916
02:44:53,050 --> 02:44:56,010
Oh my god, I see you up there, but how do I get up there?

2917
02:45:02,910 --> 02:45:05,450
I am just enchanted by this.

2918
02:45:08,130 --> 02:45:09,010
Holy shit.

2919
02:45:15,080 --> 02:45:19,020
Is this actually from the game or is it like from something else?

2920
02:45:20,080 --> 02:45:21,240
Oh, I don't want to leave.

2921
02:45:23,500 --> 02:45:24,500
Get me up, get me up.

2922
02:45:25,600 --> 02:45:27,140
Sir, sir, speak to me.

2923
02:45:29,760 --> 02:45:30,560
Okay, okay.

2924
02:45:31,660 --> 02:45:34,700
He is such a... such a musician.

2925
02:45:35,800 --> 02:45:36,280
Wow.

2926
02:45:38,520 --> 02:45:39,940
That is next level.

2927
02:45:41,800 --> 02:45:44,000
That song has no right being that good.

2928
02:45:51,380 --> 02:45:54,400
This may be one of my favorite songs in any video game ever.

2929
02:45:55,140 --> 02:45:56,440
I am just in awe.

2930
02:45:56,700 --> 02:45:58,140
It's such a simple melody.

2931
02:45:58,700 --> 02:46:00,280
What a fucking banger.

2932
02:46:03,520 --> 02:46:04,160
Wow.

2933
02:46:10,350 --> 02:46:10,990
Man.

2934
02:46:11,770 --> 02:46:13,610
Oh, I'm so happy now.

2935
02:46:13,910 --> 02:46:16,270
I just want to go around and around and around.

2936
02:46:16,750 --> 02:46:18,230
And where's the last cuckoo?

2937
02:46:19,370 --> 02:46:20,270
Maybe in here.

2938
02:46:27,110 --> 02:46:27,710
Oh.

2939
02:46:27,710 --> 02:46:28,310
God.

2940
02:46:29,150 --> 02:46:29,990
Hi, boy.

2941
02:46:30,770 --> 02:46:33,050
Is this the first time you visited this village?

2942
02:46:33,910 --> 02:46:35,810
A great woman, Impa.

2943
02:46:36,110 --> 02:46:38,410
Open up this village to us poor folk.

2944
02:46:39,190 --> 02:46:41,030
Well, make yourself at home.

2945
02:46:41,350 --> 02:46:42,910
The food isn't ready yet, though.

2946
02:46:44,230 --> 02:46:44,910
I'm scared.

2947
02:46:45,870 --> 02:46:46,910
Why do you look like...

2948
02:46:49,650 --> 02:46:57,150
I don't know what you look like, but you look like someone took your mouth and cut off a large piece of your mouth, basically.

2949
02:46:57,330 --> 02:46:58,690
You're bleeding all around the lips.

2950
02:47:00,650 --> 02:47:01,850
You've been up to no good in here.

2951
02:47:02,990 --> 02:47:04,070
That is just horrible.

2952
02:47:05,510 --> 02:47:06,310
Absolutely horrendous.

2953
02:47:11,420 --> 02:47:12,580
When is the food ready, though?

2954
02:47:18,980 --> 02:47:20,780
Man, where is that cuckoo?

2955
02:47:25,500 --> 02:47:26,820
Ah, there it is!

2956
02:47:28,460 --> 02:47:29,020
Found it!

2957
02:47:32,570 --> 02:47:33,570
That should be the last.

2958
02:47:41,330 --> 02:47:41,790
Hold on.

2959
02:47:41,870 --> 02:47:42,470
I gotta blow my nose.

2960
02:47:53,480 --> 02:47:53,920
Okay.

2961
02:47:55,200 --> 02:47:55,820
Let's go.

2962
02:47:57,740 --> 02:47:58,620
Little cuckoo!

2963
02:48:00,320 --> 02:48:03,080
Dude, I wonder if there's a quest like this in every Zelda game now.

2964
02:48:03,520 --> 02:48:04,880
Maybe it's like a recurring joke.

2965
02:48:06,780 --> 02:48:07,760
There you go, ma'am!

2966
02:48:10,400 --> 02:48:11,800
My cuckoos have...

2967
02:48:11,800 --> 02:48:12,580
run away.

2968
02:48:15,120 --> 02:48:15,860
There's more?

2969
02:48:20,220 --> 02:48:20,660
Okay.

2970
02:48:21,140 --> 02:48:22,360
Well, I did see a ladder, didn't I?

2971
02:48:23,740 --> 02:48:24,860
Let's go check out the ladder.

2972
02:48:27,900 --> 02:48:28,920
Oh, there's one!

2973
02:48:31,980 --> 02:48:33,600
I can probably get to that from the other side.

2974
02:48:36,880 --> 02:48:38,440
I hope one of them didn't fall in the well.

2975
02:48:40,060 --> 02:48:41,300
That would be most unfortunate.

2976
02:48:48,280 --> 02:48:49,600
Oh boy, they can't go here.

2977
02:48:52,500 --> 02:48:53,260
Oh wait, I saw a ladder.

2978
02:48:54,940 --> 02:48:55,620
Yeah, okay.

2979
02:48:55,960 --> 02:48:56,920
I was like, did I see a ladder?

2980
02:49:00,040 --> 02:49:01,020
Is there a cuckoo up here?

2981
02:49:02,760 --> 02:49:04,400
No way a cuckoo made his way up here, right?

2982
02:49:05,020 --> 02:49:05,980
Because that's impossible.

2983
02:49:11,300 --> 02:49:12,880
Oh my god, look at that guy.

2984
02:49:14,440 --> 02:49:16,100
There's a hole over there!

2985
02:49:16,220 --> 02:49:17,380
What is it with these weird holes?

2986
02:49:26,030 --> 02:49:27,510
I guess that leads up to the mountain.

2987
02:49:28,090 --> 02:49:28,190
Yeah.

2988
02:49:44,650 --> 02:49:44,970
Okay.

2989
02:49:47,710 --> 02:49:48,110
Down.

2990
02:49:49,610 --> 02:49:51,390
Oh, that hurt.

2991
02:49:58,310 --> 02:49:59,390
Wait, how do I...

2992
02:49:59,390 --> 02:50:01,450
Oh wait, I see a ladder on the other side here too.

2993
02:50:02,810 --> 02:50:03,610
Maybe from...

2994
02:50:03,610 --> 02:50:04,270
up here?

2995
02:50:09,750 --> 02:50:10,810
That looks impossible.

2996
02:50:10,810 --> 02:50:12,590
Unless there's a path through the house that I missed.

2997
02:50:16,050 --> 02:50:17,290
What are you hiding back there, sir?

2998
02:50:23,050 --> 02:50:23,690
Not here.

2999
02:50:24,850 --> 02:50:26,430
Wait, do I need a cuckoo to do this?

3000
02:50:32,100 --> 02:50:32,460
Oh!

3001
02:50:32,620 --> 02:50:33,340
There's another one up there!

3002
02:50:35,160 --> 02:50:37,640
So we know there's two cuckoos over in that direction now.

3003
02:50:41,270 --> 02:50:42,390
What about this house here?

3004
02:50:42,590 --> 02:50:43,050
Can we get in?

3005
02:50:49,210 --> 02:50:50,150
No door here.

3006
02:50:51,630 --> 02:50:53,170
Can I drag this fox?

3007
02:50:58,220 --> 02:50:59,740
I may need a cuckoo for this.

3008
02:51:01,120 --> 02:51:02,240
Let me go grab one.

3009
02:51:05,580 --> 02:51:06,400
Up we go.

3010
02:51:08,120 --> 02:51:08,740
Come here.

3011
02:51:14,460 --> 02:51:15,400
We go up here.

3012
02:51:18,910 --> 02:51:20,270
And now we can fly across, right?

3013
02:51:21,250 --> 02:51:21,970
Easy peasy.

3014
02:51:24,950 --> 02:51:25,990
I didn't mean to...

3015
02:51:25,990 --> 02:51:28,030
I was gonna jump with it, but...

3016
02:51:32,970 --> 02:51:34,350
Maybe I can take you up on the tower?

3017
02:51:35,590 --> 02:51:37,130
There's no way I can climb with you, though, right?

3018
02:51:38,570 --> 02:51:39,090
Hold on.

3019
02:51:40,790 --> 02:51:41,750
I gotta try.

3020
02:51:42,170 --> 02:51:45,170
Maybe he climbs with one hand, holds the cuckoo on the other.

3021
02:51:49,790 --> 02:51:52,170
I have 1% faith that this works.

3022
02:51:53,570 --> 02:51:54,550
Yeah, okay, okay.

3023
02:51:56,370 --> 02:51:57,050
Had to try.

3024
02:51:59,590 --> 02:52:00,710
We gotta get up somewhere high.

3025
02:52:06,840 --> 02:52:09,520
I'm actually unsure we can fly enough of a distance up here.

3026
02:52:15,050 --> 02:52:16,410
Yeah, there's no way we make it across.

3027
02:52:17,350 --> 02:52:18,510
Let's bring this to the graveyard.

3028
02:52:30,830 --> 02:52:31,770
Can I bring it with me?

3029
02:52:31,890 --> 02:52:32,650
I can't!

3030
02:52:33,430 --> 02:52:33,810
Okay.

3031
02:52:34,530 --> 02:52:35,770
Well, what happens to it then?

3032
02:52:37,250 --> 02:52:38,640
Is it gonna wait here for me, or...?

3033
02:52:39,910 --> 02:52:41,870
It's probably gonna be reset, that one chicken.

3034
02:52:42,710 --> 02:52:43,930
To wherever it was.

3035
02:52:45,850 --> 02:52:46,290
Shit.

3036
02:52:54,310 --> 02:52:55,170
Now to find...

3037
02:52:55,170 --> 02:52:56,030
Oh, it's that one!

3038
02:52:57,230 --> 02:52:58,230
That's so unfortunate!

3039
02:53:01,490 --> 02:53:03,450
This cuckoo situation is getting out of hand.

3040
02:53:05,870 --> 02:53:06,930
And now it's in my hand.

3041
02:53:08,750 --> 02:53:09,810
Now it's out of my hand.

3042
02:53:10,190 --> 02:53:11,310
And back on my hand.

3043
02:53:13,090 --> 02:53:16,810
She's just looking at me, thinking, what the hell is this guy doing?

3044
02:53:18,750 --> 02:53:20,590
You're not returning them, you're stealing them now!

3045
02:53:28,670 --> 02:53:29,810
Okay, now we fly across.

3046
02:53:33,250 --> 02:53:34,110
Grab this one.

3047
02:53:36,690 --> 02:53:37,310
Come on, come on!

3048
02:53:37,910 --> 02:53:38,790
Oh, that was a close one!

3049
02:53:40,970 --> 02:53:42,390
Okay, I'm just gonna try this up here now.

3050
02:53:44,530 --> 02:53:46,290
I wanna see how far I can go with it.

3051
02:53:49,550 --> 02:53:50,150
Oh, wait a minute!

3052
02:53:50,250 --> 02:53:51,070
I think I see what to do!

3053
02:53:53,630 --> 02:53:54,630
Ah, but I can't reach.

3054
02:53:55,250 --> 02:53:56,490
Maybe I can move this box.

3055
02:53:57,350 --> 02:53:58,290
Let me try this real quick.

3056
02:54:02,630 --> 02:54:03,190
Okay.

3057
02:54:05,150 --> 02:54:05,710
Hmm.

3058
02:54:07,650 --> 02:54:09,230
This is a real mystery!

3059
02:54:09,890 --> 02:54:10,850
Wait a second!

3060
02:54:13,940 --> 02:54:15,280
There's a hole in the wall up there!

3061
02:54:17,800 --> 02:54:18,740
Hold the phone!

3062
02:54:24,280 --> 02:54:25,520
I gotta check that out.

3063
02:54:30,270 --> 02:54:31,870
Okay, so I can't go around like that.

3064
02:54:43,250 --> 02:54:43,650
Oh!

3065
02:54:45,470 --> 02:54:46,850
It's where the cow is!

3066
02:54:48,230 --> 02:54:48,950
I see!

3067
02:54:49,110 --> 02:54:49,350
Okay!

3068
02:54:53,030 --> 02:54:53,950
Uh, no, no.

3069
02:54:54,030 --> 02:54:54,770
Don't play this now.

3070
02:54:57,390 --> 02:54:59,250
That lady asked you about chickens?

3071
02:54:59,450 --> 02:55:00,050
You should listen to her.

3072
02:55:00,110 --> 02:55:00,570
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

3073
02:55:01,930 --> 02:55:02,610
Chicken lady.

3074
02:55:08,350 --> 02:55:09,810
This is a real mystery here.

3075
02:55:13,550 --> 02:55:14,690
So I gotta get up there.

3076
02:55:17,470 --> 02:55:19,250
And that's not possible via the...

3077
02:55:19,250 --> 02:55:20,330
Oh, you know what?

3078
02:55:20,570 --> 02:55:22,570
We probably have to go through the windmill.

3079
02:55:24,830 --> 02:55:25,870
That's definitely it.

3080
02:55:29,980 --> 02:55:31,100
Maybe there's a door in here.

3081
02:55:31,580 --> 02:55:32,180
Higher up.

3082
02:55:34,400 --> 02:55:35,040
Whoops.

3083
02:55:43,010 --> 02:55:45,330
Oh, this music is just incredible.

3084
02:55:48,220 --> 02:55:49,720
Maybe you have to play it, actually.

3085
02:55:51,220 --> 02:55:51,840
Da-da.

3086
02:55:52,780 --> 02:55:53,720
Oh my god.

3087
02:55:55,700 --> 02:55:56,500
Da-da-da.

3088
02:55:56,820 --> 02:55:58,200
Da-da-da-da-da.

3089
02:55:58,940 --> 02:55:59,980
Da-da-da.

3090
02:56:05,220 --> 02:56:06,340
Ba-ba-ba.

3091
02:56:06,660 --> 02:56:07,140
Ba-ba-ba.

3092
02:56:07,420 --> 02:56:08,860
Ba-ba-ba.

3093
02:56:09,440 --> 02:56:10,080
Hmm.

3094
02:56:20,760 --> 02:56:21,520
That's it!

3095
02:56:23,680 --> 02:56:25,060
Uh, down, right...

3096
02:56:25,060 --> 02:56:25,340
Right?

3097
02:56:31,390 --> 02:56:32,110
I got it!

3098
02:56:35,560 --> 02:56:36,940
Ba-ba-ba, ba-ba-ba.

3099
02:56:39,640 --> 02:56:40,980
Ba-da-da-da-da-da.

3100
02:56:41,760 --> 02:56:42,940
But that's way too many notes.

3101
02:56:44,820 --> 02:56:45,220
Hmm.

3102
02:56:47,560 --> 02:56:48,480
Maybe it's this one.

3103
02:56:52,000 --> 02:56:53,280
Oh, that one works too, I guess.

3104
02:56:54,600 --> 02:56:55,000
Whoops.

3105
02:56:56,440 --> 02:56:58,260
Also, I think I have to target this guy.

3106
02:57:00,760 --> 02:57:01,400
There we go.

3107
02:57:03,420 --> 02:57:03,820
Uh.

3108
02:57:06,500 --> 02:57:07,440
Oh, that's even better!

3109
02:57:11,430 --> 02:57:11,830
Shit!

3110
02:57:15,460 --> 02:57:17,020
Also, I don't see a door in here anyway.

3111
02:57:17,180 --> 02:57:18,860
I was hoping for a door somewhere higher up.

3112
02:57:18,940 --> 02:57:20,300
So I can walk out the door.

3113
02:57:20,800 --> 02:57:22,220
And down into the other side.

3114
02:57:23,320 --> 02:57:25,080
I can't push this box, unfortunately.

3115
02:57:27,540 --> 02:57:28,400
Okay, so watch this!

3116
02:57:28,800 --> 02:57:30,460
There's a door in that house over there!

3117
02:57:31,020 --> 02:57:32,020
I see the door!

3118
02:57:36,280 --> 02:57:37,460
I also see a door here!

3119
02:57:38,220 --> 02:57:39,240
Wait a minute.

3120
02:57:39,860 --> 02:57:40,300
What?!

3121
02:57:41,180 --> 02:57:42,080
There's no way.

3122
02:57:47,390 --> 02:57:48,470
How could I have missed that?

3123
02:57:55,750 --> 02:57:56,710
There's nothing here.

3124
02:58:01,150 --> 02:58:02,330
I am so...

3125
02:58:02,790 --> 02:58:03,230
mystified!

3126
02:58:09,890 --> 02:58:10,330
Yeah.

3127
02:58:10,610 --> 02:58:12,610
Okay, I guess you can't enter that house any other way.

3128
02:58:14,390 --> 02:58:15,710
Maybe we can target this guy up here.

3129
02:58:18,510 --> 02:58:19,390
Oh, there we go!

3130
02:58:21,370 --> 02:58:22,430
I can't get down!

3131
02:58:22,630 --> 02:58:23,590
So all I can do...

3132
02:58:23,590 --> 02:58:24,830
is look at Death Mountain.

3133
02:58:26,310 --> 02:58:27,110
Well, that's...

3134
02:58:27,110 --> 02:58:27,710
a conundrum.

3135
02:58:28,750 --> 02:58:29,750
I'm sorry to hear that.

3136
02:58:35,680 --> 02:58:37,020
I know there's a door here!

3137
02:58:38,940 --> 02:58:39,900
Get out of the way, sir!

3138
02:58:41,360 --> 02:58:42,640
I know you're hiding a door.

3139
02:58:44,920 --> 02:58:46,080
Uh, let me go this way now.

3140
02:58:48,980 --> 02:58:50,760
The road is closed beyond this point.

3141
02:58:51,240 --> 02:58:52,520
Can't you read the sign over there?

3142
02:58:52,720 --> 02:58:53,760
I'm sorry I missed it.

3143
02:58:54,160 --> 02:58:54,420
Eh?

3144
02:58:54,940 --> 02:58:55,840
Oh, I see.

3145
02:58:56,000 --> 02:58:56,900
You're just a kid.

3146
02:58:57,320 --> 02:58:58,420
And you can't read yet.

3147
02:58:58,760 --> 02:58:59,060
Ha ha.

3148
02:58:59,340 --> 02:58:59,460
Ha.

3149
02:59:00,240 --> 02:59:00,680
Wow.

3150
02:59:00,880 --> 02:59:02,040
I can read fine.

3151
02:59:02,700 --> 02:59:03,140
Alright.

3152
02:59:03,420 --> 02:59:05,260
I know my A's and B's and C's.

3153
02:59:06,240 --> 02:59:06,780
Death Mountain.

3154
02:59:06,920 --> 02:59:08,480
No passage without a royal decree.

3155
02:59:09,740 --> 02:59:10,180
Ah!

3156
02:59:11,220 --> 02:59:12,580
Well, wait a minute.

3157
02:59:13,560 --> 02:59:15,060
I believe I have that.

3158
02:59:16,660 --> 02:59:19,320
I have the royalist of all of the decrees.

3159
02:59:21,660 --> 02:59:22,720
Look at that.

3160
02:59:23,220 --> 02:59:23,780
Oh!

3161
02:59:23,940 --> 02:59:24,940
This is...

3162
02:59:24,940 --> 02:59:27,300
This is surely Princess Zelda's handwriting.

3163
02:59:27,720 --> 02:59:28,600
Well, let's see.

3164
02:59:28,780 --> 02:59:28,980
Hmm.

3165
02:59:30,020 --> 02:59:30,380
Okay.

3166
02:59:31,400 --> 02:59:32,560
This is Link.

3167
02:59:32,860 --> 02:59:35,160
He is under my orders to save Hyrule.

3168
02:59:38,640 --> 02:59:41,520
What kind of funny game has our princess come up with now?

3169
02:59:42,820 --> 02:59:43,260
Okay.

3170
02:59:43,480 --> 02:59:43,720
Okay.

3171
02:59:43,860 --> 02:59:44,040
Alright.

3172
02:59:44,440 --> 02:59:45,220
You can go now.

3173
02:59:45,520 --> 02:59:46,880
Just be careful, Mr. Hero.

3174
02:59:47,520 --> 02:59:48,160
Ha ha ha ha.

3175
02:59:49,280 --> 02:59:50,940
I mean, I would react the same way.

3176
02:59:50,980 --> 02:59:51,600
That is silly.

3177
02:59:53,560 --> 02:59:58,580
That is pretty much the McLovin' of this universe, you know?

3178
02:59:58,580 --> 03:00:00,300
By the way, Mr. Hero.

3179
03:00:01,320 --> 03:00:05,300
If you're going to climb Death Mountain, you should equip a proper shield.

3180
03:00:05,680 --> 03:00:07,480
It is an active volcano, after all.

3181
03:00:08,560 --> 03:00:12,620
If you go back to Hyrule Castle, town market, you should check out the bazaar.

3182
03:00:12,840 --> 03:00:14,100
They sell the shield you need there.

3183
03:00:15,220 --> 03:00:15,880
You know what?

3184
03:00:16,140 --> 03:00:17,440
That's a good, uh...

3185
03:00:17,440 --> 03:00:18,680
That's a good suggestion there.

3186
03:00:19,180 --> 03:00:21,300
Tell them I sent you and they should give you a special discount.

3187
03:00:21,460 --> 03:00:21,940
Oh, fuck.

3188
03:00:23,480 --> 03:00:26,280
If you think you're good to go already, don't worry about it.

3189
03:00:27,140 --> 03:00:29,100
Now, I'd like to ask a favor of you.

3190
03:00:29,520 --> 03:00:32,940
No, I don't expect you to do it just because of the great tip I just gave you.

3191
03:00:33,220 --> 03:00:34,160
I'm just asking.

3192
03:00:35,340 --> 03:00:39,400
Have you been to the Happy Mask shop that just opened in the Hyrule Castle town market?

3193
03:00:40,000 --> 03:00:41,160
Everyone is talking about it.

3194
03:00:41,540 --> 03:00:42,940
I have, and it's weird AF.

3195
03:00:44,440 --> 03:00:48,800
My little boy posters me for a popular mask, but I don't have time to go there.

3196
03:00:49,840 --> 03:00:53,200
So, could you go and get the mask for me next time you're in the market?

3197
03:00:53,840 --> 03:00:58,480
If you don't feel like it, that's okay, but, well, I have no choice.

3198
03:00:58,700 --> 03:00:59,620
This is my job.

3199
03:01:03,280 --> 03:01:05,200
I don't think you want to go there, man.

3200
03:01:05,300 --> 03:01:06,200
That place is weird.

3201
03:01:06,440 --> 03:01:07,980
I'm getting bad vibes from it.

3202
03:01:08,280 --> 03:01:09,400
You should not go there.

3203
03:01:11,260 --> 03:01:15,120
Also, I have the shield already, you know.

3204
03:01:16,000 --> 03:01:16,220
Whoops.

3205
03:01:23,130 --> 03:01:23,850
There we go.

3206
03:01:26,980 --> 03:01:27,860
Check me out.

3207
03:01:29,580 --> 03:01:33,080
I wish I could go to the mask shop in town to buy a present for my kid.

3208
03:01:34,300 --> 03:01:34,640
Ah.

3209
03:01:35,840 --> 03:01:36,560
I know.

3210
03:01:36,840 --> 03:01:37,720
Sounds like a struggle.

3211
03:01:38,780 --> 03:01:39,820
Let's just head up here.

3212
03:01:40,560 --> 03:01:41,680
The cuckoos can wait.

3213
03:01:46,850 --> 03:01:47,910
Death Mountain Trail.

3214
03:01:54,140 --> 03:01:54,820
All right.

3215
03:01:56,420 --> 03:01:58,240
That is a evil creature.

3216
03:01:59,160 --> 03:02:00,200
We shall murder it.

3217
03:02:00,600 --> 03:02:00,900
Hi-ya!

3218
03:02:01,740 --> 03:02:02,360
Oh, jump.

3219
03:02:03,080 --> 03:02:03,860
Let me try again.

3220
03:02:05,300 --> 03:02:05,740
Just...

3221
03:02:05,740 --> 03:02:06,300
Hi-ya!

3222
03:02:06,640 --> 03:02:07,540
There we go.

3223
03:02:07,660 --> 03:02:08,820
Look at that crabby crab.

3224
03:02:09,780 --> 03:02:11,000
Going the way of the dodo.

3225
03:02:14,120 --> 03:02:14,560
Boink!

3226
03:02:14,940 --> 03:02:15,560
Oh, my God.

3227
03:02:17,020 --> 03:02:17,900
There we go.

3228
03:02:18,220 --> 03:02:18,740
Nailed it.

3229
03:02:18,840 --> 03:02:19,600
This here is a secret.

3230
03:02:22,570 --> 03:02:23,570
Something's moving in there, too.

3231
03:02:23,590 --> 03:02:24,050
I can hear it.

3232
03:02:25,630 --> 03:02:26,190
Oh, my God.

3233
03:02:26,290 --> 03:02:26,570
The jump.

3234
03:02:29,070 --> 03:02:29,690
There we go.

3235
03:02:30,590 --> 03:02:32,010
Wait, why do I have the royal decree?

3236
03:02:33,170 --> 03:02:33,530
Equipped.

3237
03:02:35,490 --> 03:02:36,110
There we go.

3238
03:02:40,010 --> 03:02:40,630
Excuse me.

3239
03:02:42,450 --> 03:02:42,810
Boom.

3240
03:02:45,290 --> 03:02:45,950
You like that?

3241
03:02:50,110 --> 03:02:51,210
Uh, there's a heart up there.

3242
03:02:53,230 --> 03:02:53,590
Oh!

3243
03:02:54,910 --> 03:02:55,610
Oh, my God.

3244
03:02:55,610 --> 03:02:56,190
It's a Gorok.

3245
03:02:58,270 --> 03:02:58,630
Hey!

3246
03:03:00,710 --> 03:03:02,030
I am one of the Gor...

3247
03:03:02,030 --> 03:03:02,810
Oh, Gorons, right.

3248
03:03:03,290 --> 03:03:05,510
The stone-eating people who live on Death Mountain.

3249
03:03:05,890 --> 03:03:08,250
Man, you look exactly like the people from Breath of the Wild.

3250
03:03:10,890 --> 03:03:13,210
Why would they steal all that from Breath of the Wild, you know?

3251
03:03:13,810 --> 03:03:15,490
Look at that huge boulder over there.

3252
03:03:16,490 --> 03:03:19,210
It blocks the entrance to the Dodongo's cavern.

3253
03:03:19,610 --> 03:03:22,110
Which was once a very important place for us Gorons.

3254
03:03:23,010 --> 03:03:23,790
Why once?

3255
03:03:24,350 --> 03:03:28,010
But one day, many Dodongo suddenly appeared inside the cavern.

3256
03:03:28,290 --> 03:03:29,990
It became a very dangerous place.

3257
03:03:31,090 --> 03:03:36,750
On top of that, a Gerudo in black armor used his magic to seal the entrance with that boulder.

3258
03:03:38,610 --> 03:03:39,750
Black magic, you say?

3259
03:03:39,910 --> 03:03:40,190
No, no.

3260
03:03:40,310 --> 03:03:40,810
Black armor.

3261
03:03:40,910 --> 03:03:41,270
Okay, okay.

3262
03:03:41,350 --> 03:03:41,590
Never mind.

3263
03:03:42,810 --> 03:03:46,530
If you want to hear more Goron gossip, head up to our city.

3264
03:03:47,450 --> 03:03:47,890
GG.

3265
03:03:49,390 --> 03:03:51,390
Goron City is just a little way up the trail.

3266
03:03:51,750 --> 03:03:53,570
It won't take much longer to get out there.

3267
03:03:53,830 --> 03:03:54,610
Even on foot.

3268
03:03:56,370 --> 03:03:56,770
Okay.

3269
03:03:59,150 --> 03:04:01,490
You want to hear more Goron gossip, head up to our city.

3270
03:04:02,790 --> 03:04:03,930
I will, I will, I will.

3271
03:04:07,330 --> 03:04:07,730
Money!

3272
03:04:07,970 --> 03:04:08,450
Oh, that's a lot.

3273
03:04:09,610 --> 03:04:10,330
We got 82.

3274
03:04:10,570 --> 03:04:10,810
We're rich.

3275
03:04:12,250 --> 03:04:13,170
The Dodongo's cavern.

3276
03:04:13,430 --> 03:04:14,550
Don't enter without permission.

3277
03:04:16,050 --> 03:04:17,390
I mean, I can't, right?

3278
03:04:17,530 --> 03:04:18,330
Because everything's blocked.

3279
03:04:19,850 --> 03:04:21,470
Dude, I'm getting rich from these.

3280
03:04:22,470 --> 03:04:23,690
There's riches in them hills.

3281
03:04:27,810 --> 03:04:29,150
Every one of them had three gems.

3282
03:04:30,130 --> 03:04:30,530
Incredible.

3283
03:04:37,800 --> 03:04:39,040
I could become a Goron.

3284
03:04:39,560 --> 03:04:40,740
I think I have what it takes.

3285
03:04:41,020 --> 03:04:41,700
I could go pro.

3286
03:04:50,180 --> 03:04:51,040
That's a Goron.

3287
03:04:54,180 --> 03:04:57,380
They say that a beautiful fairy lives on top of Death Mountain.

3288
03:04:58,600 --> 03:04:59,600
Don't you want to see her?

3289
03:05:00,960 --> 03:05:02,340
I would love to see her.

3290
03:05:03,360 --> 03:05:04,880
Was he scratching his butt just now?

3291
03:05:07,220 --> 03:05:07,700
Okay.

3292
03:05:12,130 --> 03:05:16,270
Follow the trail along the edge of the cliff and you will reach Goron City, home of the Gorons.

3293
03:05:18,170 --> 03:05:19,130
Yeah, sure.

3294
03:05:19,510 --> 03:05:20,770
What about I say no to that?

3295
03:05:20,970 --> 03:05:21,310
I mean...

3296
03:05:22,030 --> 03:05:22,510
Wow.

3297
03:05:23,890 --> 03:05:24,370
Link!

3298
03:05:25,170 --> 03:05:25,990
You're embarrassing.

3299
03:05:28,070 --> 03:05:29,290
I can't cut the sign?

3300
03:05:29,450 --> 03:05:29,850
Why not?

3301
03:05:34,060 --> 03:05:35,000
Death Mountain Trail.

3302
03:05:38,660 --> 03:05:39,180
Oh!

3303
03:05:39,420 --> 03:05:40,680
Wait, I don't understand.

3304
03:05:40,920 --> 03:05:41,520
What's down here then?

3305
03:05:43,980 --> 03:05:44,980
Oh, Death.

3306
03:05:47,740 --> 03:05:48,940
Can I actually jump down?

3307
03:05:54,190 --> 03:05:55,170
Wait a second.

3308
03:05:56,470 --> 03:05:56,990
Oh!

3309
03:05:57,630 --> 03:05:58,410
Hello there!

3310
03:06:01,440 --> 03:06:02,420
Where are you going?

3311
03:06:10,150 --> 03:06:10,630
Sir?

3312
03:06:13,630 --> 03:06:15,430
That was an interesting maneuver you got there.

3313
03:06:16,630 --> 03:06:20,670
I wish I could roll down the mountain like a rock with a bomb flower and...

3314
03:06:21,670 --> 03:06:22,150
Boom!

3315
03:06:23,510 --> 03:06:27,070
If I could do that with a bomb flower, I could become a real man.

3316
03:06:28,110 --> 03:06:35,130
Or you could, you know, walk along the catwalks in Kokoriki Village and you will become a real man.

3317
03:06:35,670 --> 03:06:37,270
That's what the lady there told me anyway.

3318
03:06:38,230 --> 03:06:39,270
I'm a real boy!

3319
03:06:40,990 --> 03:06:42,390
Okay, I think I see what's happening here.

3320
03:06:42,470 --> 03:06:45,750
We gotta give him some kind of flower and he will roll down here and destroy that boulder for us.

3321
03:06:47,050 --> 03:06:47,610
Got it.

3322
03:06:49,010 --> 03:06:50,070
I'll find explosives.

3323
03:06:50,550 --> 03:06:51,230
No problem.

3324
03:06:58,120 --> 03:06:58,680
Look at this.

3325
03:06:58,720 --> 03:06:59,620
Another place we can open.

3326
03:07:14,130 --> 03:07:14,530
Hello!

3327
03:07:17,640 --> 03:07:20,600
I'm standing here to shade the bomb flowers from the sun.

3328
03:07:21,960 --> 03:07:23,460
Do you have a question for me?

3329
03:07:24,720 --> 03:07:26,720
I would like to ask about the bomb flowers.

3330
03:07:28,140 --> 03:07:30,460
Those plants growing over there are bomb flowers.

3331
03:07:30,840 --> 03:07:33,600
They are mining plants that grow only on this mountain.

3332
03:07:34,560 --> 03:07:37,320
They usually grow only in dark places, like caves.

3333
03:07:37,700 --> 03:07:40,740
So bomb flowers that grow in a place like this are extremely rare.

3334
03:07:41,620 --> 03:07:46,380
If you have the Goron's bracelet, even a little kid like you could easily pick it with A.

3335
03:07:47,700 --> 03:07:48,680
You don't say...

3336
03:07:50,180 --> 03:07:50,860
Bracelet, eh?

3337
03:07:50,860 --> 03:07:53,240
Natural wonder, bomb flower, danger.

3338
03:07:53,560 --> 03:07:54,240
Do not uproot.

3339
03:08:03,280 --> 03:08:03,740
Okay.

3340
03:08:06,180 --> 03:08:07,420
We gotta test these things.

3341
03:08:10,900 --> 03:08:11,780
What do you got for me?

3342
03:08:12,860 --> 03:08:14,480
Impa said that the spi- Shut up!

3343
03:08:16,720 --> 03:08:17,960
Don't you see I'm working on it?

3344
03:08:19,380 --> 03:08:20,280
Am I not here?

3345
03:08:21,160 --> 03:08:21,620
Hello?

3346
03:08:27,230 --> 03:08:27,690
Money!

3347
03:08:30,650 --> 03:08:31,750
Dude, I can buy anything.

3348
03:08:47,070 --> 03:08:47,890
Look at all that!

3349
03:08:48,130 --> 03:08:48,910
Oh my god, they're disappearing.

3350
03:08:54,380 --> 03:08:54,780
Wait.

3351
03:08:55,460 --> 03:08:56,620
I can't get to a hundred?

3352
03:08:59,320 --> 03:09:00,320
It's stuck on 99!

3353
03:09:01,900 --> 03:09:02,900
What the hell is this?

3354
03:09:04,020 --> 03:09:04,860
Okay, wait a second.

3355
03:09:05,480 --> 03:09:06,520
I'm gonna go up over here.

3356
03:09:14,330 --> 03:09:15,350
Let's see what we got here.

3357
03:09:18,410 --> 03:09:19,210
Oh, steep mountain.

3358
03:09:19,530 --> 03:09:20,130
Come on, Link.

3359
03:09:20,870 --> 03:09:21,550
You strong boy.

3360
03:09:23,590 --> 03:09:24,370
Mountain Summit.

3361
03:09:24,570 --> 03:09:25,110
Danger ahead.

3362
03:09:25,230 --> 03:09:25,530
Keep out.

3363
03:09:26,790 --> 03:09:27,230
Right.

3364
03:09:28,030 --> 03:09:28,970
There's no danger.

3365
03:09:30,170 --> 03:09:31,150
Oh, I need bombs.

3366
03:09:31,970 --> 03:09:32,730
I see...

3367
03:09:32,730 --> 03:09:33,330
I see your stance.

3368
03:09:34,350 --> 03:09:35,170
Wait, what do you want?

3369
03:09:38,210 --> 03:09:39,410
What does it mean when it's green?

3370
03:09:43,110 --> 03:09:44,490
Navi, what does it mean when you're green?

3371
03:09:47,410 --> 03:09:48,410
Speak to me, Navi.

3372
03:09:54,560 --> 03:09:55,280
Here we go.

3373
03:09:55,380 --> 03:09:55,940
This is the city.

3374
03:09:58,100 --> 03:09:59,220
Land of the Gorons.

3375
03:09:59,680 --> 03:10:00,380
Goron City.

3376
03:10:01,420 --> 03:10:02,560
Filled with Gorons.

3377
03:10:11,580 --> 03:10:12,100
Hello.

3378
03:10:14,980 --> 03:10:16,740
Oh, I'm so hungry.

3379
03:10:18,260 --> 03:10:21,620
Everyone feels faint from hunger because of the food shortage in this town.

3380
03:10:22,080 --> 03:10:23,400
We're in danger of extinction.

3381
03:10:24,400 --> 03:10:25,320
That's not good.

3382
03:10:26,100 --> 03:10:28,020
It's all because we can't enter our quarry.

3383
03:10:28,320 --> 03:10:29,440
The Dodongo's Cavern.

3384
03:10:30,420 --> 03:10:32,340
We Gorons live on a diet of rocks.

3385
03:10:32,880 --> 03:10:34,080
Yeah, that is kind of messed up.

3386
03:10:34,080 --> 03:10:38,540
And the most delicious and nutritious rocks around are found in the Dodongo's Cavern.

3387
03:10:39,020 --> 03:10:40,840
But that seems like ancient history now.

3388
03:10:41,960 --> 03:10:46,060
We've become such gourmets that we can't stand to eat rocks from anywhere else.

3389
03:10:46,700 --> 03:10:47,220
Wow.

3390
03:10:48,320 --> 03:10:52,260
I want to eat at the top sirloin rocks from the Dodongo's Cavern.

3391
03:10:54,740 --> 03:10:56,860
What determines a good rock?

3392
03:10:58,680 --> 03:11:00,120
The taste of a rock.

3393
03:11:02,420 --> 03:11:04,280
You know what the worst rock would be to taste?

3394
03:11:05,360 --> 03:11:06,440
You know what it would be.

3395
03:11:09,990 --> 03:11:11,410
Dude, I play so much Ark Raiders.

3396
03:11:11,570 --> 03:11:15,470
My instinct every time I go down a surface like this is to roll or slide.

3397
03:11:16,250 --> 03:11:17,210
And I can't slide.

3398
03:11:17,990 --> 03:11:18,390
Slide!

3399
03:11:21,930 --> 03:11:23,390
This is such a silly song.

3400
03:11:32,150 --> 03:11:33,210
That seems dangerous.

3401
03:11:34,750 --> 03:11:35,290
Ow!

3402
03:11:35,710 --> 03:11:37,090
Hey, watch where you're going, buddy!

3403
03:11:38,730 --> 03:11:39,890
Come on, get out of there.

3404
03:11:40,250 --> 03:11:40,790
Stop rolling.

3405
03:11:45,490 --> 03:11:46,030
Mother!

3406
03:11:46,410 --> 03:11:46,890
Come here.

3407
03:11:49,530 --> 03:11:50,270
Stand still.

3408
03:11:53,610 --> 03:11:54,450
Where are you?

3409
03:11:57,480 --> 03:11:58,420
Oh, you bastard.

3410
03:12:00,800 --> 03:12:01,480
What's this?

3411
03:12:02,560 --> 03:12:04,920
If you can stop my wild rolling, you might get something great.

3412
03:12:05,360 --> 03:12:06,280
Hot Rodder Goron!

3413
03:12:07,660 --> 03:12:08,700
You don't say.

3414
03:12:11,800 --> 03:12:12,660
What do I have?

3415
03:12:13,840 --> 03:12:16,640
I could try and stun him with my nuts.

3416
03:12:18,300 --> 03:12:19,740
That'll stop him in his tracks.

3417
03:12:25,580 --> 03:12:25,980
No?

3418
03:12:30,210 --> 03:12:30,950
Oh, man!

3419
03:12:33,690 --> 03:12:35,290
Okay, it's gonna be like that, huh?

3420
03:12:36,550 --> 03:12:37,610
I'm going down here, then.

3421
03:12:45,050 --> 03:12:45,410
Heading...

3422
03:12:45,410 --> 03:12:45,490
Oh.

3423
03:12:46,690 --> 03:12:47,290
Wait, what?

3424
03:12:47,910 --> 03:12:49,290
I'm looking at the map right now.

3425
03:12:50,170 --> 03:12:50,830
Oh, okay.

3426
03:12:50,970 --> 03:12:51,930
So this is like a way around.

3427
03:12:58,300 --> 03:12:59,260
So now we're up here.

3428
03:13:00,660 --> 03:13:01,660
Let's go to the center.

3429
03:13:07,950 --> 03:13:08,350
Whoa!

3430
03:13:09,470 --> 03:13:09,910
Hey!

3431
03:13:11,910 --> 03:13:12,850
What's happening, buddy?

3432
03:13:13,650 --> 03:13:14,090
Hey!

3433
03:13:14,950 --> 03:13:17,670
It's dangerous for a little kid like you to come out here.

3434
03:13:18,050 --> 03:13:19,130
You might fall down.

3435
03:13:20,130 --> 03:13:23,190
If I'm not mistaken, you came out here to eat the red stone.

3436
03:13:23,590 --> 03:13:25,090
Well, too bad it's not here.

3437
03:13:25,950 --> 03:13:26,350
What?

3438
03:13:26,910 --> 03:13:27,910
That's not why you're here?

3439
03:13:28,990 --> 03:13:31,170
You're looking for a spiritual stone?

3440
03:13:31,730 --> 03:13:35,010
You must mean that delicious-looking red stone that was once displayed here.

3441
03:13:35,990 --> 03:13:40,330
I was so hungry that I thought it would be okay to just give it one tiny little lick.

3442
03:13:40,770 --> 03:13:41,850
So I snuck out here.

3443
03:13:42,250 --> 03:13:43,430
But it was already gone.

3444
03:13:44,630 --> 03:13:46,170
I think Big Brother took it away.

3445
03:13:47,050 --> 03:13:49,750
He always says that everyone is after that red stone.

3446
03:13:50,830 --> 03:13:52,450
I need that stone, sir.

3447
03:13:53,170 --> 03:13:57,890
Big Brother has shut himself up in his room saying, I will wait in here for the royal family's messenger.

3448
03:13:58,750 --> 03:14:00,210
That's awfully convenient.

3449
03:14:01,250 --> 03:14:02,310
Because look what I got.

3450
03:14:03,110 --> 03:14:04,530
I got a royal decree.

3451
03:14:06,290 --> 03:14:06,910
Check it.

3452
03:14:07,990 --> 03:14:08,470
Boom!

3453
03:14:10,510 --> 03:14:11,270
Not impressed?

3454
03:14:11,550 --> 03:14:11,830
Alright.

3455
03:14:12,790 --> 03:14:15,370
I guess I'll show it to the guy who wants to see it.

3456
03:14:16,490 --> 03:14:19,030
Someone who actually appreciates stuff like this.

3457
03:14:21,770 --> 03:14:22,750
Hey, yo, watch this.

3458
03:14:41,920 --> 03:14:42,320
Damn!

3459
03:14:44,360 --> 03:14:45,240
Oh, wait a second.

3460
03:14:45,300 --> 03:14:46,260
Maybe I need to...

3461
03:14:50,050 --> 03:14:50,450
No?

3462
03:14:51,070 --> 03:14:52,490
I thought that would blow up or something.

3463
03:14:53,750 --> 03:14:54,370
You there!

3464
03:14:55,590 --> 03:14:56,750
Oh, I need flame!

3465
03:14:57,810 --> 03:14:58,470
Of course.

3466
03:14:59,650 --> 03:15:01,550
Big Brother has shut himself up in his room.

3467
03:15:01,550 --> 03:15:04,670
saying, I will wait in here for the royal family's messenger.

3468
03:15:05,030 --> 03:15:07,850
His name is most likely Link, and he's wearing a cool shield.

3469
03:15:09,090 --> 03:15:10,170
Yeah, he's talking about me.

3470
03:15:12,090 --> 03:15:13,090
How do I get fire?

3471
03:15:22,680 --> 03:15:23,680
A heart!

3472
03:15:24,140 --> 03:15:24,580
A heart!

3473
03:15:27,130 --> 03:15:28,150
A stick!

3474
03:15:29,640 --> 03:15:30,350
I need that.

3475
03:15:31,810 --> 03:15:32,370
No?

3476
03:15:33,130 --> 03:15:35,370
We don't get many visitors way up here.

3477
03:15:35,870 --> 03:15:36,530
Where are you from?

3478
03:15:37,630 --> 03:15:38,410
The forest?

3479
03:15:39,310 --> 03:15:40,750
What's a forest?

3480
03:15:41,890 --> 03:15:42,370
Eh?

3481
03:15:43,510 --> 03:15:46,870
It's where a lot of trees and plants grow.

3482
03:15:48,330 --> 03:15:49,830
Now I'm even more confused.

3483
03:15:50,330 --> 03:15:52,710
Nothing grows around here besides the bomb flowers.

3484
03:15:53,970 --> 03:15:56,550
We don't have seeds or nuts around here either.

3485
03:15:58,010 --> 03:16:00,170
Even Deku sticks are very scarce around here.

3486
03:16:01,570 --> 03:16:02,990
I know a trick to conserve sticks.

3487
03:16:03,410 --> 03:16:05,830
If you light a stick on fire, it will burn to ashes.

3488
03:16:06,590 --> 03:16:08,430
Press A to put it away before it completely burns.

3489
03:16:09,110 --> 03:16:09,690
Oh yeah!

3490
03:16:09,890 --> 03:16:10,230
Good tip.

3491
03:16:11,050 --> 03:16:12,710
By the way, I hit a stick somewhere.

3492
03:16:13,830 --> 03:16:14,690
What in your butt?

3493
03:16:17,110 --> 03:16:18,230
Why did you laugh like that?

3494
03:16:19,290 --> 03:16:20,330
That made me uncomfortable.

3495
03:16:22,050 --> 03:16:23,290
No, stop playing that.

3496
03:16:23,670 --> 03:16:25,030
I do not command you to do so.

3497
03:16:26,550 --> 03:16:31,050
I think I need to light this candle on top of that pot or urn.

3498
03:16:33,790 --> 03:16:34,850
Lovely cave drawings.

3499
03:16:35,870 --> 03:16:36,750
Dancing morons.

3500
03:16:36,910 --> 03:16:37,670
I mean, gorons.

3501
03:16:40,830 --> 03:16:42,450
Man, how do I get fire?

3502
03:16:47,630 --> 03:16:48,930
You will tell me, won't you?

3503
03:16:53,350 --> 03:16:55,970
I'm so hungry that I can't think about anything but food.

3504
03:16:57,150 --> 03:16:57,990
Spiritual stone?

3505
03:16:58,950 --> 03:17:01,050
That red stone that was lighting up our city.

3506
03:17:02,370 --> 03:17:04,330
Big brother Darumia took it away.

3507
03:17:05,230 --> 03:17:07,470
Then he shut himself up in his room and won't come out.

3508
03:17:08,530 --> 03:17:11,690
Since then it feels like all the lights in the city have gone out.

3509
03:17:12,430 --> 03:17:14,670
Everyone seems so depressed.

3510
03:17:16,150 --> 03:17:19,010
I want you to bring fire from Big Brother's room back here.

3511
03:17:19,750 --> 03:17:20,250
Aha!

3512
03:17:22,170 --> 03:17:23,070
Is that in here?

3513
03:17:25,170 --> 03:17:25,670
Wait.

3514
03:17:28,270 --> 03:17:29,490
Oh my god.

3515
03:17:29,630 --> 03:17:31,630
Is this a shortcut to the lost forest?

3516
03:17:34,790 --> 03:17:35,890
There's no way.

3517
03:17:38,290 --> 03:17:39,490
These are the rocks!

3518
03:17:43,530 --> 03:17:44,170
Aha!

3519
03:17:45,650 --> 03:17:47,810
Ba-da-da-da-da-da-da-da.

3520
03:17:48,870 --> 03:17:51,130
Ba-da-ba-da-ba-ba.

3521
03:17:52,450 --> 03:17:53,970
Yeah, where's Big Brother's room?

3522
03:17:54,110 --> 03:17:54,710
Sorry, I missed it.

3523
03:17:54,770 --> 03:17:55,410
Can you tell me again?

3524
03:17:58,580 --> 03:18:00,320
Big Brother's room back here.

3525
03:18:05,050 --> 03:18:06,690
I mean... okay.

3526
03:18:09,150 --> 03:18:10,370
This is very confusing.

3527
03:18:11,930 --> 03:18:14,750
So on the mini-map there, there's definitely a room to the north.

3528
03:18:14,910 --> 03:18:17,310
That's the room where we need to go, ultimately.

3529
03:18:18,450 --> 03:18:20,750
But then there's also rooms to the left and right.

3530
03:18:20,930 --> 03:18:22,150
I don't think I've been there yet.

3531
03:18:24,170 --> 03:18:26,630
And to do that, we've got to get upstairs first, I think.

3532
03:18:29,210 --> 03:18:30,530
So around like this.

3533
03:18:34,060 --> 03:18:35,640
Up here, and then we take a left.

3534
03:18:36,640 --> 03:18:38,220
Oh, there's rocks in the way!

3535
03:18:39,320 --> 03:18:40,220
Actually, we're fine.

3536
03:18:40,320 --> 03:18:41,700
We can walk along these...

3537
03:18:44,000 --> 03:18:44,480
chains?

3538
03:18:45,780 --> 03:18:46,500
Or wood.

3539
03:18:47,160 --> 03:18:48,360
What is this called?

3540
03:18:48,500 --> 03:18:49,560
Like a knot.

3541
03:18:51,460 --> 03:18:52,180
Twirled wood.

3542
03:19:00,050 --> 03:19:00,530
Nice!

3543
03:19:01,310 --> 03:19:01,950
Nailed it.

3544
03:19:05,130 --> 03:19:06,530
Is this where the fire resides?

3545
03:19:08,750 --> 03:19:09,450
Oh no.

3546
03:19:13,280 --> 03:19:14,120
It says grab.

3547
03:19:19,140 --> 03:19:19,860
It's not working.

3548
03:19:26,470 --> 03:19:26,830
What?

3549
03:19:34,750 --> 03:19:36,010
Let's try going to the right side.

3550
03:19:43,750 --> 03:19:44,390
Oh man.

3551
03:19:46,130 --> 03:19:46,930
Hey dude, get away!

3552
03:19:48,790 --> 03:19:49,150
Oh!

3553
03:19:49,530 --> 03:19:50,430
Almost pushed me off.

3554
03:19:50,990 --> 03:19:51,090
Oh!

3555
03:19:51,270 --> 03:19:53,090
Link, link, link, link, link, link, link, link, link, link, link, link, link.

3556
03:19:54,890 --> 03:19:56,170
Oh wait, I could have just walked here.

3557
03:19:57,310 --> 03:19:58,210
What do we have down here?

3558
03:20:00,450 --> 03:20:01,610
Oh, that looks fiery.

3559
03:20:02,510 --> 03:20:03,170
Looks doable.

3560
03:20:07,070 --> 03:20:07,470
Oh!

3561
03:20:08,030 --> 03:20:08,350
Careful.

3562
03:20:40,020 --> 03:20:40,420
Okay.

3563
03:20:43,200 --> 03:20:45,220
Maybe I just need to have the stick out, because it's so hot in here?

3564
03:20:51,430 --> 03:20:52,110
Catch fire.

3565
03:21:14,920 --> 03:21:15,460
Broke it.

3566
03:21:18,890 --> 03:21:20,330
Okay, I'm not sure what to do here.

3567
03:21:20,450 --> 03:21:21,930
What the fuck is going on?

3568
03:21:23,330 --> 03:21:24,430
What else do I have here?

3569
03:21:26,130 --> 03:21:26,690
Uh, no.

3570
03:21:26,850 --> 03:21:27,410
Didn't mean to do that.

3571
03:21:40,360 --> 03:21:41,580
I am so lost.

3572
03:21:41,580 --> 03:21:42,800
I actually have no idea what to do.

3573
03:21:47,330 --> 03:21:48,450
Sorry, can you remind me?

3574
03:21:53,390 --> 03:21:53,730
Uh...

3575
03:21:54,150 --> 03:21:54,490
Right.

3576
03:21:54,790 --> 03:21:56,010
I want to eat rocks.

3577
03:22:01,650 --> 03:22:03,730
I guess we've got to find a way to stop that guy from rolling.

3578
03:22:05,770 --> 03:22:07,370
That's probably the main thing right now.

3579
03:22:08,630 --> 03:22:09,610
So how do we do that?

3580
03:22:11,170 --> 03:22:12,250
What items do we have?

3581
03:22:12,530 --> 03:22:13,850
We can try and sing him a song.

3582
03:22:20,300 --> 03:22:21,760
Or maybe try to hit him from the front.

3583
03:22:40,040 --> 03:22:41,060
Let me hit you with my stick.

3584
03:22:47,960 --> 03:22:48,340
Dammit!

3585
