03:55:18,510 --> 03:55:19,990
There's something back here I can do.

4145
03:55:34,670 --> 03:55:36,590
Did this guy sell a bomb thingy?

4146
03:55:42,520 --> 03:55:42,920
Uh...

4147
03:55:43,640 --> 03:55:44,300
I don't...

4148
03:55:44,300 --> 03:55:45,200
No, I don't think you did.

4149
03:55:47,280 --> 03:55:48,800
I mean, I can try and buy bombs.

4150
03:55:50,760 --> 03:55:52,100
Let's try and buy five bombs.

4151
03:55:53,680 --> 03:55:54,460
I'm sorry.

4152
03:55:54,700 --> 03:55:56,080
That bomb is just for display.

4153
03:55:56,380 --> 03:55:57,940
I'm sold out of real ones.

4154
03:56:01,130 --> 03:56:02,190
Well, you asshole.

4155
03:56:04,970 --> 03:56:05,450
That's...

4156
03:56:05,450 --> 03:56:07,210
Why would you put it on display then, you psycho?

4157
03:56:10,310 --> 03:56:11,130
Speak to me, man.

4158
03:56:13,830 --> 03:56:16,630
I'm so hungry that I can't think about anything but food.

4159
03:56:20,730 --> 03:56:23,150
If he's in a bad mood, you'll probably get mad at you.

4160
03:56:23,990 --> 03:56:25,010
It can be pretty scary.

4161
03:56:25,370 --> 03:56:25,730
But...

4162
03:56:26,250 --> 03:56:27,330
I know his secret.

4163
03:56:27,470 --> 03:56:27,830
Oh, yeah?

4164
03:56:29,170 --> 03:56:32,490
He may not look like the type, but Big Brother loves to dance.

4165
03:56:32,990 --> 03:56:35,250
If he gets in a rhythm, he'll surely...

4166
03:56:36,630 --> 03:56:40,330
I remember Big Brother used to always listen to the music that comes from the forest.

4167
03:56:40,550 --> 03:56:41,650
Oh, shit!

4168
03:56:42,490 --> 03:56:42,950
Ah, yes.

4169
03:56:43,270 --> 03:56:44,150
The good old days.

4170
03:56:44,510 --> 03:56:46,290
That music makes me feel nostalgic, too.

4171
03:56:47,530 --> 03:56:51,570
When all the torches on this floor are lit, Goron City is really lively.

4172
03:56:52,850 --> 03:56:54,430
Brother, man, say no more.

4173
03:56:55,570 --> 03:56:56,530
Say no more.

4174
03:56:57,790 --> 03:56:58,810
I got it, fam.

4175
03:57:00,490 --> 03:57:00,970
Uh...

4176
03:57:01,610 --> 03:57:02,410
Look at my stick.

4177
03:57:03,590 --> 03:57:04,330
Now it's gone.

4178
03:57:05,250 --> 03:57:05,950
Look at my stick.

4179
03:57:06,590 --> 03:57:07,630
And gone.

4180
03:57:08,270 --> 03:57:09,950
But that's not what I wanted to show you.

4181
03:57:11,290 --> 03:57:12,370
Check this out.

4182
03:57:21,680 --> 03:57:22,760
There it is.

4183
03:57:24,540 --> 03:57:26,980
La la la la la la...

4184
03:57:29,530 --> 03:57:31,410
No, I...

4185
03:57:31,410 --> 03:57:32,770
No.

4186
03:57:33,950 --> 03:57:34,670
Really?

4187
03:57:35,150 --> 03:57:36,990
Then do you want to talk to me?

4188
03:57:39,490 --> 03:57:40,210
What?

4189
03:57:40,930 --> 03:57:41,650
Yes?

4190
03:57:43,450 --> 03:57:44,170
Imposite...

4191
03:57:44,170 --> 03:57:44,510
No!

4192
03:58:00,430 --> 03:58:01,290
Come on, please.

4193
03:58:01,690 --> 03:58:02,630
There it is!

4194
03:58:09,180 --> 03:58:10,220
Oh my god!

4195
03:58:18,790 --> 03:58:20,490
He's vibing so hard.

4196
03:58:20,490 --> 03:58:21,330
It's sick.

4197
03:58:21,870 --> 03:58:23,390
He's got the stank face on.

4198
03:58:23,510 --> 03:58:23,650
Look!

4199
03:58:26,210 --> 03:58:27,850
Come on, come on, come on!

4200
03:58:28,130 --> 03:58:28,550
Hot!

4201
03:58:29,630 --> 03:58:30,730
What a hot beat!

4202
03:58:42,630 --> 03:58:43,030
Oh.

4203
03:58:44,030 --> 03:58:45,350
Hey, what a nice tune!

4204
03:58:46,990 --> 03:58:49,150
Just like that, my depression is all gone.

4205
03:58:49,730 --> 03:58:50,790
Something just came over me.

4206
03:58:50,990 --> 03:58:52,610
I suddenly wanted to dance like crazy.

4207
03:58:53,050 --> 03:58:54,850
Okay, from now, I'm gonna buy a flute.

4208
03:58:55,390 --> 03:58:58,610
Go to my friends when they feel bad, and just play that tune in front of their faces.

4209
03:58:58,930 --> 03:59:00,830
And then go, Feels good, doesn't it?

4210
03:59:00,930 --> 03:59:01,710
And then leave again.

4211
03:59:02,790 --> 03:59:04,050
I am Darunia.

4212
03:59:05,070 --> 03:59:06,930
I'm the big boss of the Gorons.

4213
03:59:07,450 --> 03:59:09,410
Was there something you wanted to ask me about?

4214
03:59:10,450 --> 03:59:10,950
What?

4215
03:59:12,110 --> 03:59:14,510
You want the spiritual stone of fire, too?

4216
03:59:15,570 --> 03:59:20,470
The spiritual stone of fire, also known as the Gorons' ruby, is our race's hidden treasure.

4217
03:59:21,350 --> 03:59:22,130
But hold on.

4218
03:59:22,350 --> 03:59:24,250
I'm not gonna give it to you that easily.

4219
03:59:24,690 --> 03:59:25,930
If you want it so badly.

4220
03:59:26,610 --> 03:59:31,570
Why don't you go destroy the monsters inside of the Dodongo's cavern and prove you're a real man?

4221
03:59:32,930 --> 03:59:35,490
That way, everybody will be happy again.

4222
03:59:35,690 --> 03:59:38,270
If you do it, I will give you anything you want.

4223
03:59:38,570 --> 03:59:39,810
Even the spiritual stone.

4224
03:59:41,050 --> 03:59:42,190
I have something for you.

4225
03:59:42,550 --> 03:59:45,330
I'm not really giving you this in return for anything.

4226
03:59:45,570 --> 03:59:46,510
But take it anyway.

4227
03:59:47,930 --> 03:59:52,010
If you wear this, even a little fella like you can pick a bomb flower using A.

4228
03:59:52,210 --> 03:59:53,450
Oh, let's go!

4229
03:59:56,480 --> 03:59:58,160
You got the Gorons' bracelet.

4230
03:59:58,540 --> 04:00:00,400
Now you can pull up bomb flowers.

4231
04:00:00,940 --> 04:00:02,900
Stand next to one and use A to pull it up.

4232
04:00:04,160 --> 04:00:04,880
Heck yeah!

4233
04:00:07,890 --> 04:00:11,410
Destroy the monsters in the Dodongo's cavern and become a real man.

4234
04:00:11,930 --> 04:00:14,010
Then we can talk about the spiritual stone.

4235
04:00:15,150 --> 04:00:15,810
Got it.

4236
04:00:16,490 --> 04:00:16,790
Alright.

4237
04:00:17,510 --> 04:00:18,810
Well, I'm all for that.

4238
04:00:18,810 --> 04:00:19,490
Let me save the game.

4239
04:00:21,570 --> 04:00:22,370
There you go.

4240
04:00:26,170 --> 04:00:26,810
That's it!

4241
04:00:27,250 --> 04:00:27,910
We're done!

4242
04:00:29,350 --> 04:00:30,210
We are done.

4243
04:00:33,450 --> 04:00:34,430
That's it for today.

4244
04:00:35,990 --> 04:00:37,710
Because I need food as well.

4245
04:00:37,970 --> 04:00:40,370
All that talk of delicious rocks made me hungry.

4246
04:00:42,270 --> 04:00:45,330
Dude, that scene with the guy dancing was actually amazing.

4247
04:00:46,090 --> 04:00:49,390
The stank face he had on and the seriousness in his face.

4248
04:00:49,470 --> 04:00:51,210
You could really feel he was feeling it.

4249
04:00:53,730 --> 04:00:54,450
It was great.

4250
04:00:57,650 --> 04:00:59,030
I'm not gonna eat rocks now.

4251
04:00:59,190 --> 04:00:59,550
Come on.

4252
04:01:04,640 --> 04:01:05,260
What's for dinner?

4253
04:01:05,400 --> 04:01:06,140
I don't know, actually.

4254
04:01:06,180 --> 04:01:07,140
I don't have anything prepared.

4255
04:01:07,300 --> 04:01:08,220
I need to go buy something.

4256
04:01:09,440 --> 04:01:11,180
The worst rock to eat would be diorite.

4257
04:01:11,260 --> 04:01:11,740
You got it!

4258
04:01:12,220 --> 04:01:12,540
Nice!

4259
04:01:12,640 --> 04:01:13,460
That's what I was thinking of.

4260
04:01:14,640 --> 04:01:15,700
But you do eat salt.

4261
04:01:15,880 --> 04:01:16,540
Oh, come on!

4262
04:01:16,700 --> 04:01:17,180
Okay, fine.

4263
04:01:17,380 --> 04:01:17,780
You got me.

4264
04:01:19,600 --> 04:01:19,880
True.

4265
04:01:20,220 --> 04:01:24,180
I guess I also drink water, which is a little rocky these days.

4266
04:01:24,500 --> 04:01:25,560
At least in my area.

4267
04:01:25,900 --> 04:01:26,740
It's a little hard.

4268
04:01:28,680 --> 04:01:29,480
Diet siorite.

4269
04:01:29,840 --> 04:01:31,880
That sounds delicious, actually.

4270
04:01:32,500 --> 04:01:33,840
You're not gonna get fat from it.

4271
04:01:34,980 --> 04:01:35,840
First time here, Oliver?

4272
04:01:35,840 --> 04:01:36,680
What's up, Jujoya?

4273
04:01:37,160 --> 04:01:37,920
What's going on?

4274
04:01:38,800 --> 04:01:39,600
Good to have you.

4275
04:01:42,510 --> 04:01:44,910
We shall not start a debate on rocks versus minerals.

4276
04:01:45,710 --> 04:01:46,670
Yeah, Marie.

4277
04:01:48,990 --> 04:01:51,870
Maybe if you learn the taste, you can identify diorite easier.

4278
04:01:52,970 --> 04:01:57,150
I mean, I remember people in the geology department, they would lick rocks all the time.

4279
04:01:57,630 --> 04:01:58,510
I'm not even kidding.

4280
04:01:59,050 --> 04:02:00,250
Like, that's what they would do.

4281
04:02:02,390 --> 04:02:03,410
Those kids were weird.

4282
04:02:06,210 --> 04:02:06,870
Weird times.

4283
04:02:08,870 --> 04:02:11,670
I mean, I did it too for a while, but then I realized it was bad.

4284
04:02:13,070 --> 04:02:14,050
I'm not actually kidding.

4285
04:02:14,250 --> 04:02:14,830
This is real.

4286
04:02:16,290 --> 04:02:17,550
I don't know why they did it.

4287
04:02:18,770 --> 04:02:20,210
Maybe it was like a meme or something.

4288
04:02:20,370 --> 04:02:21,450
Like a real life meme.

4289
04:02:22,510 --> 04:02:22,870
Plutonium.

4290
04:02:27,400 --> 04:02:28,540
What about rock candy?

4291
04:02:28,580 --> 04:02:29,280
I don't know what that is.

4292
04:02:29,620 --> 04:02:30,920
Oh, you're talking about...

4293
04:02:32,800 --> 04:02:33,640
Oh, what's the word?

4294
04:02:35,620 --> 04:02:38,620
The sweet rocks that you lick until they become small.

4295
04:02:39,900 --> 04:02:40,580
You know what I mean?

4296
04:02:41,940 --> 04:02:43,740
How are you enjoying this 90s children's game?

4297
04:02:43,860 --> 04:02:44,480
Pretty easy.

4298
04:02:46,520 --> 04:02:46,920
Listen.

4299
04:02:47,820 --> 04:02:49,560
Children had it hard in the 90s, all right?

4300
04:02:49,620 --> 04:02:50,020
I would know.

4301
04:02:50,120 --> 04:02:50,760
I'm a 90s kid.

4302
04:02:51,700 --> 04:02:53,600
I played my fair share of games, all right?

4303
04:02:53,760 --> 04:02:55,920
Like, I did play Super Mario 64 back then.

4304
04:02:56,360 --> 04:02:58,500
I never completed it because it was that hard.

4305
04:02:59,580 --> 04:03:01,740
The whole family had trouble, you know?

4306
04:03:01,740 --> 04:03:04,380
We never did find all the stars to this day.

4307
04:03:04,720 --> 04:03:07,160
We haven't found all the stars in Super Mario 64.

4308
04:03:10,330 --> 04:03:11,770
You rocked the predictions today?

4309
04:03:12,130 --> 04:03:13,710
Wait, what did you guys predict?

4310
04:03:14,030 --> 04:03:15,390
Like, what kind of predictions did you make?

4311
04:03:15,510 --> 04:03:16,110
I'm curious.

4312
04:03:17,230 --> 04:03:18,630
What would you make predictions about?

4313
04:03:23,030 --> 04:03:24,430
You troll us with the songs?

4314
04:03:25,470 --> 04:03:27,790
I have not been trolling at all today.

4315
04:03:29,790 --> 04:03:31,590
Hand on the heart, I swear to you.

4316
04:03:32,270 --> 04:03:34,630
I am just not very good at remembering the combinations.

4317
04:03:37,250 --> 04:03:39,410
When you got lost on the song, when you would get it.

4318
04:03:42,010 --> 04:03:45,450
You do realize that could mean any number of instances today.

4319
04:03:47,770 --> 04:03:49,490
That could be any time in this dream.

4320
04:03:50,750 --> 04:03:52,470
Will you do a Spyro blind playthrough?

4321
04:03:52,550 --> 04:03:53,750
I have played Spyro before.

4322
04:03:57,150 --> 04:03:58,530
But there's multiple Spyros.

4323
04:03:58,650 --> 04:04:00,790
I don't actually remember if I played more than one.

4324
04:04:01,510 --> 04:04:03,590
But I definitely played Spyro as a kid.

4325
04:04:05,630 --> 04:04:08,110
I love how you said, when in doubt, play a song.

4326
04:04:08,230 --> 04:04:09,250
And immediately didn't do it.

4327
04:04:09,310 --> 04:04:09,550
Oh yeah.

4328
04:04:09,830 --> 04:04:10,810
Oh, I guess so, actually.

4329
04:04:10,890 --> 04:04:11,230
That's true.

4330
04:04:15,920 --> 04:04:18,740
I did beat Mario 64, but gave up on Mario Sunshine.

4331
04:04:19,040 --> 04:04:19,840
I haven't played that either.

4332
04:04:20,980 --> 04:04:22,960
I also want to play Super Mario Galaxy.

4333
04:04:23,400 --> 04:04:25,160
But that was on the Wii, I think.

4334
04:04:25,940 --> 04:04:28,480
Maybe that's been remastered for Switch or something.

4335
04:04:31,540 --> 04:04:32,500
I mean, I guess, yeah.

4336
04:04:32,820 --> 04:04:34,300
I got lost a couple times today.

4337
04:04:34,840 --> 04:04:36,620
But honestly, I'm expecting that.

4338
04:04:36,620 --> 04:04:39,140
Because that's just how old games are made, you know?

4339
04:04:40,060 --> 04:04:41,400
They're a little difficult.

4340
04:04:41,400 --> 04:04:45,580
It's not always easy to figure out what the next step is.

4341
04:04:48,500 --> 04:04:49,480
You mean Wii Master?

4342
04:04:50,320 --> 04:04:50,760
Nice.

4343
04:04:51,540 --> 04:04:52,380
Wii Master.

4344
04:04:55,820 --> 04:04:58,560
Did you feel so break-brained today trying to remember the music notes?

4345
04:04:58,680 --> 04:05:00,540
I mean, it's weird.

4346
04:05:00,560 --> 04:05:03,060
Because they give you three examples, right?

4347
04:05:03,720 --> 04:05:08,860
And then during the last example, for some reason, my brain just stops working.

4348
04:05:09,580 --> 04:05:11,800
And I think of something completely unrelated.

4349
04:05:12,540 --> 04:05:13,600
And then I lost it.

4350
04:05:13,880 --> 04:05:15,700
So when it actually comes to...

4351
04:05:15,700 --> 04:05:21,040
When the time comes to, you know, put on a performance there and actually do the notes, then I can't remember it.

4352
04:05:22,560 --> 04:05:23,980
It's a weird fumble.

4353
04:05:29,220 --> 04:05:31,520
Say Mar-E-O, not Mario.

4354
04:05:31,880 --> 04:05:32,500
Oh, Mario.

4355
04:05:33,340 --> 04:05:33,860
Oh!

4356
04:05:34,800 --> 04:05:35,320
Okay.

4357
04:05:37,000 --> 04:05:39,200
So it's not Mar-E-Lago, it's Mar-E-Lago.

4358
04:05:44,040 --> 04:05:45,520
Actually, it's nothing to do with the audience.

4359
04:05:45,700 --> 04:05:47,680
It's the same without an audience.

4360
04:05:49,160 --> 04:05:54,600
When I try to pay attention to something and it's time to perform in any way, I always...

4361
04:05:54,600 --> 04:05:55,620
Okay, that sounded weird now.

4362
04:05:55,800 --> 04:05:56,660
But you know what I mean?

4363
04:05:56,780 --> 04:06:06,680
Like, if it's like a combination of things I need to remember, also combine that with me not being very good with notes and all that and musical stuff, just made it a difficult cocktail there.

4364
04:06:09,420 --> 04:06:11,520
Next stream is Speedrunning Mario 64, right?

4365
04:06:11,700 --> 04:06:14,000
Dude, I would actually love to play more old games.

4366
04:06:15,600 --> 04:06:17,940
I'm having such a blast with this.

4367
04:06:19,400 --> 04:06:21,840
I definitely am going to play more old games.

4368
04:06:24,640 --> 04:06:26,320
Why are you so thirsty for Saria?

4369
04:06:26,380 --> 04:06:27,440
I just like her hair, okay?

4370
04:06:28,620 --> 04:06:29,620
Her hair is cool.

4371
04:06:33,910 --> 04:06:35,130
And definitely memorable.

4372
04:06:35,390 --> 04:06:37,850
I will never not mistake it for any other type of hair.

4373
04:06:40,410 --> 04:06:41,210
Crash Bandicoot?

4374
04:06:41,290 --> 04:06:44,090
I actually did play one of the Crash Bandicoots as a child.

4375
04:06:44,930 --> 04:06:47,650
I had fun with it, but I didn't play all of them, I don't think.

4376
04:06:50,310 --> 04:06:50,710
Malon?

4377
04:06:51,070 --> 04:06:51,470
Saria?

4378
04:06:52,510 --> 04:06:53,130
No way.

4379
04:07:01,260 --> 04:07:02,460
It happened to me on Monday.

4380
04:07:02,620 --> 04:07:04,040
Everything went blank during a presentation.

4381
04:07:04,680 --> 04:07:05,080
Yeah, right?

4382
04:07:05,240 --> 04:07:06,020
Stuff like that.

4383
04:07:08,100 --> 04:07:09,520
What's with these five-second ads?

4384
04:07:09,640 --> 04:07:10,360
I don't know.

4385
04:07:10,940 --> 04:07:12,260
I have no control over that.

4386
04:07:12,360 --> 04:07:16,140
I only control how many ads per hour are being played, not the specific ads.

4387
04:07:17,480 --> 04:07:20,600
Have you noticed any inspirations from this game for Miyazaki?

4388
04:07:23,300 --> 04:07:25,200
I guess the combat system is very similar.

4389
04:07:25,740 --> 04:07:29,100
I don't know if this is at all related.

4390
04:07:33,310 --> 04:07:34,070
The music...

4391
04:07:34,070 --> 04:07:34,370
Oh my god.

4392
04:07:34,510 --> 04:07:36,150
Guys, the music in the windmill.

4393
04:07:39,220 --> 04:07:39,980
Holy shit!

4394
04:07:40,720 --> 04:07:42,820
That will be a banger forever for me.

4395
04:07:44,700 --> 04:07:46,380
It is so good.

4396
04:07:48,580 --> 04:07:49,860
Like, I can't say that enough.

4397
04:07:52,120 --> 04:07:55,000
I wish they put it in an area where you had to listen to it more.

4398
04:07:58,210 --> 04:07:59,510
Such a great song.

4399
04:08:03,780 --> 04:08:06,900
Goated, it's greatest of all, all the times.

4400
04:08:08,720 --> 04:08:11,180
Like, it is in a league of its own.

4401
04:08:13,480 --> 04:08:14,900
Just so incredible.

4402
04:08:15,840 --> 04:08:19,600
This game pioneered Lock-On, which so many other games adopted.

4403
04:08:19,800 --> 04:08:20,360
Oh, really?

4404
04:08:20,440 --> 04:08:21,100
Was this the first?

4405
04:08:23,060 --> 04:08:24,500
That's an interesting bit of trivia.

4406
04:08:26,340 --> 04:08:27,800
